# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Abbrev-Concepts.html
msgid ""
"An <em class=\"dfn\">abbrev</em> is a word that has been defined to <em "
"class=\"dfn\">expand</em> into a specified <em class=\"dfn\">expansion</"
"em>.  When you insert a word-separator character following the abbrev, that "
"expands the abbrev&mdash;replacing the abbrev with its expansion.  For "
"example, if &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">foo</samp>&rsquo; is defined as an "
"abbrev expanding to &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">find outer otter</"
"samp>&rsquo;, then typing <kbd class=\"kbd\">f o o .</kbd> will insert "
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">find outer otter.</samp>&rsquo;."
msgstr ""
"<em class=\"dfn\">略語</em>とは、指定された<em class=\"dfn\">展開形</em>に"
"<em class=\"dfn\">展開</em>されるように定義された単語のことです。略語の後に単"
"語区切り文字を入力すると、その略語が展開され、略語が展開形に置き換えられま"
"す。例えば、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">foo</samp>&rsquo;が&lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">find outer otter</samp>&rsquo;に展開する略語として定義されてい"
"る場合、<kbd class=\"kbd\">f o o .</kbd>と入力すると&lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">find outer otter.</samp>&rsquo;が挿入されます。"

