# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><h4>
#: build/html/emacs/Adaptive-Fill.html
msgid ""
"<span>27.6.4 Adaptive Filling<a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#Adaptive-"
"Filling\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span>27.6.4 適応的塗りつぶし<a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#Adaptive-"
"Filling\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/emacs/Adaptive-Fill.html
msgid "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-adaptive-filling\"></a>"
msgstr "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-adaptive-filling\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Adaptive-Fill.html
msgid ""
"The fill commands can deduce the proper fill prefix for a paragraph "
"automatically in certain cases: either whitespace or certain punctuation "
"characters at the beginning of a line are propagated to all lines of the "
"paragraph."
msgstr ""
"フィルコマンドは、特定のケースにおいて、段落に適したフィルプレフィックスを自"
"動的に推論できます。具体的には、行頭の空白や特定の句読点文字が、段落内のすべ"
"ての行に伝播されます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Adaptive-Fill.html
msgid ""
"If the paragraph has two or more lines, the fill prefix is taken from the "
"paragraph&rsquo;s second line, but only if it appears on the first line as "
"well."
msgstr ""
"段落が2行以上ある場合、フィルプレフィックスは段落の2行目から取得されますが、"
"これは1行目にも含まれている場合に限ります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Adaptive-Fill.html
msgid ""
"If a paragraph has just one line, fill commands <em class=\"emph\">may</em> "
"take a prefix from that line.  The decision is complicated because there are "
"three reasonable things to do in such a case:"
msgstr ""
"段落が1行のみの場合、fillコマンドは<em class=\"emph\">その行</em>をプレフィッ"
"クスとして受け取ることがあります。このようなケースでは妥当な処理が3通りあるた"
"め、判断が複雑になります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li>
#: build/html/emacs/Adaptive-Fill.html
msgid "Use the first line&rsquo;s prefix on all the lines of the paragraph."
msgstr "段落のすべての行に、1行目の接頭辞を付けてください。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li>
#: build/html/emacs/Adaptive-Fill.html
msgid ""
"Indent subsequent lines with whitespace, so that they line up under the text "
"that follows the prefix on the first line, but don&rsquo;t actually copy the "
"prefix from the first line."
msgstr ""
"後続の行を空白でインデントし、1行目のプレフィックスに続くテキストの下に揃うよ"
"うにしますが、1行目のプレフィックス自体は実際にコピーしないでください。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li>
#: build/html/emacs/Adaptive-Fill.html
msgid "Don&rsquo;t do anything special with the second and following lines."
msgstr "2行目以降は、特に何もしないでください。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Adaptive-Fill.html
msgid ""
"All three of these styles of formatting are commonly used.  So the fill "
"commands try to determine what you would like, based on the prefix that "
"appears and on the major mode.  Here is how."
msgstr ""
"これら3つの書式スタイルはいずれも一般的に使用されています。そのため、フィルコ"
"マンドは、表示されるプレフィックスとメジャーモードに基づいて、ユーザーが何を"
"意図しているかを判断しようとします。その仕組みは以下の通りです。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/emacs/Adaptive-Fill.html
msgid ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-"
"adaptive_002dfill_002dfirst_002dline_002dregexp\"></a>"
msgstr ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-"
"adaptive_002dfill_002dfirst_002dline_002dregexp\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Adaptive-Fill.html
msgid ""
"If the prefix found on the first line matches <code class=\"code\">adaptive-"
"fill-first-line-regexp</code>, or if it appears to be a comment-starting "
"sequence (this depends on the major mode), then the prefix found is used for "
"filling the paragraph, provided it would not act as a paragraph starter on "
"subsequent lines."
msgstr ""
"1行目で見つかったプレフィックスが <code class=\"code\">adaptive-fill-first-"
"line-regexp</code> と一致するか、あるいはコメント開始シーケンスであると思われ"
"る場合（これはメジャーモードによって異なります）、そのプレフィックスは、後続"
"の行で段落の開始記号として機能しない限り、段落の埋め合わせに使用されます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Adaptive-Fill.html
msgid ""
"Otherwise, the prefix found is converted to an equivalent number of spaces, "
"and those spaces are used as the fill prefix for the rest of the lines, "
"provided they would not act as a paragraph starter on subsequent lines."
msgstr ""
"それ以外の場合、見つかった接頭辞は同等の数のスペースに変換され、それらのス"
"ペースは、後続の行で段落の開始文字として機能しない限り、残りの行の埋め草頭辞"
"として使用されます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Adaptive-Fill.html
msgid ""
"In Text mode, and other modes where only blank lines and page delimiters "
"separate paragraphs, the prefix chosen by adaptive filling never acts as a "
"paragraph starter, so it can always be used for filling."
msgstr ""
"テキストモードや、空行とページ区切りのみで段落が区切られるその他のモードで"
"は、適応型フィルが選択する接頭辞が段落の開始記号として機能することはないた"
"め、常にフィルに使用できます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/emacs/Adaptive-Fill.html
msgid ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-adaptive_002dfill_002dmode\"></a> <a "
"class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-adaptive_002dfill_002dregexp\"></a>"
msgstr ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-adaptive_002dfill_002dmode\"></a> <a "
"class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-adaptive_002dfill_002dregexp\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Adaptive-Fill.html
msgid ""
"The variable <code class=\"code\">adaptive-fill-regexp</code> determines "
"what kinds of line beginnings can serve as a fill prefix: any characters at "
"the start of the line that match this regular expression are used.  If you "
"set the variable <code class=\"code\">adaptive-fill-mode</code> to <code "
"class=\"code\">nil</code>, the fill prefix is never chosen automatically."
msgstr ""
"変数 <code class=\"code\">adaptive-fill-regexp</code> は、どのような種類の行"
"頭がフィルプレフィックスとして機能できるかを決定します。行頭にある文字のう"
"ち、この正規表現に一致するものがすべて使用されます。変数 <code "
"class=\"code\">adaptive-fill-mode</code> を <code class=\"code\">nil</code> "
"に設定すると、フィルプレフィックスが自動的に選択されることはなくなります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/emacs/Adaptive-Fill.html
msgid ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-adaptive_002dfill_002dfunction\"></a>"
msgstr ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-adaptive_002dfill_002dfunction\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Adaptive-Fill.html
msgid ""
"You can specify more complex ways of choosing a fill prefix automatically by "
"setting the variable <code class=\"code\">adaptive-fill-function</code> to a "
"function.  This function is called with point after the left margin of a "
"line, and it should return the appropriate fill prefix based on that line.  "
"If it returns <code class=\"code\">nil</code>, <code class=\"code\">adaptive-"
"fill-regexp</code> gets a chance to find a prefix."
msgstr ""
"変数 <code class=\"code\">adaptive-fill-function</code> に関数を設定すること"
"で、フィルプレフィックスを自動的に選択するためのより複雑な方法を指定できま"
"す。この関数は、行の左マージン以降のポイントを引数として呼び出され、その行に"
"基づいて適切なフィルプレフィックスを返す必要があります。もし <code "
"class=\"code\">nil</code> が返された場合、<code class=\"code\">adaptive-fill-"
"regexp</code> がプレフィックスを探す機会を得ます。"

