msgstr "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-dissociated_002dpress\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Amusements.html
msgid ""
"<kbd class=\"kbd\">M-x dissociated-press</kbd> scrambles the text in the "
"current Emacs buffer, word by word or character by character, writing its "
"output to a buffer named <samp class=\"file\">*Dissociation*</samp>.  A "
"positive argument tells it to operate character by character, and specifies "
"the number of overlap characters.  A negative argument tells it to operate "
"word by word, and specifies the number of overlap words.  Dissociated Press "
"produces results fairly like those of a Markov chain, but is however, an "
"independent, ignoriginal invention; it techniquitously copies several "
"consecutive characters from the sample text between random jumps, unlike a "
"Markov chain which would jump randomly after each word or character.  Keep "
"dissociwords out of your documentation, if you want it to be well userenced "
"and properbose."
msgstr ""
"<kbd class=\"kbd\">M-x dissociated-press</kbd> は、現在の Emacs バッファ内の"
"テキストを単語単位または文字単位でスクランブルし、その出力を <samp "
"class=\"file\">*Dissociation*</samp> という名前のバッファに書き込みます。正の"
"引数を指定すると文字単位で処理が行われ、重複する文字数が指定されます。負の引"
"数を指定すると単語単位で処理が行われ、重複する単語数が指定されます。"
"Dissociated Press はマルコフ連鎖にかなり近い結果を生成しますが、独立した独創"
"的な発明です。単語や文字ごとにランダムにジャンプするマルコフ連鎖とは異なり、"
"ランダムなジャンプの合間に、サンプルテキストから連続する数文字を技術的にコ"
"ピーします。ドキュメントを十分に参照可能で適切に保ちたいのであれば、"
"dissociwords は含めないようにしてください。"

