# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><h4>
#: build/html/emacs/Auto-Reverting-Dired.html
msgid ""
"<span>20.5.1.2 Auto Reverting Dired buffers<a class=\"copiable-link\" "
"href=\"#Auto-Reverting-Dired-buffers\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span>20.5.1.2 Diredバッファの自動リバート<a class=\"copiable-link\" "
"href=\"#Auto-Reverting-Dired-buffers\"> &para;</a></span>"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Auto-Reverting-Dired.html
msgid ""
"Dired buffers only auto-revert when the file list of the buffer&rsquo;s main "
"directory changes (e.g., when a new file is added or deleted).  They do not "
"auto-revert when information about a particular file changes (e.g., when the "
"size changes) or when inserted subdirectories change.  To be sure that <em "
"class=\"emph\">all</em> listed information is up to date, you have to "
"manually revert using <kbd class=\"kbd\">g</kbd>, <em class=\"emph\">even</"
"em> if auto-reverting is enabled in the Dired buffer.  Sometimes, you might "
"get the impression that modifying or saving files listed in the main "
"directory actually does cause auto-reverting.  This is because making "
"changes to a file, or saving it, very often causes changes in the directory "
"itself; for instance, through backup files or auto-save files.  However, "
"this is not guaranteed."
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Auto-Reverting-Dired.html
msgid ""
"If the Dired buffer is marked modified and there are no changes you want to "
"protect, then most of the time you can make auto-reverting resume by "
"manually reverting the buffer using <kbd class=\"kbd\">g</kbd>.  There is "
"one exception.  If you flag or mark files, you can safely revert the "
"buffer.  This will not erase the flags or marks (unless the marked file has "
"been deleted, of course).  However, the buffer will stay modified, even "
"after reverting, and auto-reverting will not resume.  This is because, if "
"you flag or mark files, you may be working on the buffer and you might not "
"want the buffer to change without warning.  If you want auto-reverting to "
"resume in the presence of marks and flags, mark the buffer non-modified "
"using <kbd class=\"kbd\">M-~</kbd>.  However, adding, deleting or changing "
"marks or flags will mark it modified again."
msgstr ""
"Diredバッファが変更済みとしてマークされており、かつ保護したい変更がない場合"
"は、ほとんどの場合、<kbd class=\"kbd\">g</kbd> を使用して手動でバッファをリ"
"バートすることで、自動リバートを再開できます。ただし、1点例外があります。ファ"
"イルにフラグやマークを付けている場合は、安全にバッファをリバートできます。こ"
"れにより、フラグやマークが消去されることはありません（もちろん、マークした"
"ファイルが削除されている場合は除きます）。しかし、リバート後もバッファは変更"
"済みのままとなり、自動リバートは再開されません。これは、ファイルにフラグや"
"マークを付けている場合、バッファを操作している最中であり、予告なくバッファが"
"変更されることを望まない可能性があるためです。マークやフラグがある状態でも自"
"動リバートを再開させたい場合は、<kbd class=\"kbd\">M-~</kbd> を使用してバッ"
"ファを未変更としてマークしてください。ただし、マークやフラグを追加、削除、ま"
"たは変更すると、再び変更済みとしてマークされます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Auto-Reverting-Dired.html
msgid ""
"Remote Dired buffers are currently not auto-reverted.  Neither are Dired "
"buffers for which you used shell wildcards or file arguments to list only "
"some of the files.  <samp class=\"file\">*Find*</samp> and <samp "
"class=\"file\">*Locate*</samp> buffers do not auto-revert either."
msgstr ""
"リモートのDiredバッファは、現在自動リバートされません。シェルのワイルドカード"
"やファイル引数を使用して一部のファイルのみを一覧表示したDiredバッファも同様で"
"す。<samp class=\"file\">*Find*</samp> および <samp class=\"file\">*Locate*</"
"samp> バッファも自動リバートされません。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Auto-Reverting-Dired.html
msgid ""
