#: build/html/emacs/Calendar-Systems.html
msgid ""
"Astronomers use a simple counting of days elapsed since noon, Monday, "
"January 1, 4713 BC on the Julian calendar.  The number of days elapsed since "
"then is called the <em class=\"dfn\">Julian day number</em> or the <em "
"class=\"dfn\">Astronomical day number</em>."
msgstr ""
"天文学者は、ユリウス暦の紀元前4713年1月1日（月）正午から経過した日数を単純に"
"数える。それ以降に経過した日数は、<em class=\"dfn\">ユリウス日</em>または<em "
"class=\"dfn\">天文日</em>と呼ばれる。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/emacs/Calendar-Systems.html
msgid "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-Hebrew-calendar\"></a>"
msgstr "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-Hebrew-calendar\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Calendar-Systems.html
msgid ""
"The Hebrew calendar is used by tradition in the Jewish religion.  The Emacs "
"calendar program uses the Hebrew calendar to determine the dates of Jewish "
"holidays.  Hebrew calendar dates begin and end at sunset."
msgstr ""
"ユダヤ教では、伝統的にヘブライ暦が用いられています。Emacsのカレンダープログラ"
"ムは、ユダヤ教の祝日の日付を算出するためにヘブライ暦を使用しています。ヘブラ"
"イ暦の日付は、日没に始まり、日没に終わります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/emacs/Calendar-Systems.html
msgid "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-Islamic-calendar\"></a>"
msgstr "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-Islamic-calendar\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Calendar-Systems.html
msgid ""
"The Islamic calendar is used in many predominantly Islamic countries.  Emacs "
"uses it to determine the dates of Islamic holidays.  There is no universal "
"agreement in the Islamic world about the calendar; Emacs uses a widely "
"accepted version, but the precise dates of Islamic holidays often depend on "
"proclamation by religious authorities, not on calculations.  As a "
"consequence, the actual dates of observance can vary slightly from the dates "
"computed by Emacs.  Islamic calendar dates begin and end at sunset."
msgstr ""
"イスラム暦は、イスラム教徒が多数を占める多くの国で使用されています。Emacsはこ"
"の暦を用いて、イスラム教の祝日の日付を決定します。イスラム世界においてこの暦"
"に関する普遍的な合意はなく、Emacsは広く受け入れられている版を採用しています"
"が、イスラム教の祝日の正確な日付は、計算ではなく宗教当局による布告に依存する"
"ことがよくあります。その結果、実際の遵守日は、Emacsが算出した日付とわずかに異"
"なる場合があります。イスラム暦の日付は、日没に始まり、日没に終わります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/emacs/Calendar-Systems.html
msgid ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-French-Revolutionary-calendar\"></a>"
msgstr ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-French-Revolutionary-calendar\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Calendar-Systems.html
msgid ""
"The French Revolutionary calendar was created by the Jacobins after the 1789 "
"revolution, to represent a more secular and nature-based view of the annual "
"cycle, and to install a 10-day week in a rationalization measure similar to "
"the metric system.  The French government officially abandoned this calendar "
"at the end of 1805."
msgstr ""
"フランス革命暦は、1789年の革命後、より世俗的で自然に基づいた年間周期の捉え方"
"を提示し、メートル法と同様の合理化策として10日週を導入するため、ジャコバン派"
"によって制定された。フランス政府は1805年末に、この暦を正式に廃止した。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/emacs/Calendar-Systems.html
msgid ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-Mayan-calendars\"></a> <a "
"class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-long-count-calendar-system\"></a> <a "
"class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-tzolkin-calendar-system\"></a> <a "
"class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-haab-calendar-system\"></a> <a "
"class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-Goodman_002dMartinez_002dThompson-"
"correlation\"></a>"
msgstr ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-Mayan-calendars\"></a> <a "
"class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-long-count-calendar-system\"></a> <a "
"class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-tzolkin-calendar-system\"></a> <a "
"class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-haab-calendar-system\"></a> <a "
"class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-Goodman_002dMartinez_002dThompson-"
"correlation\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Calendar-Systems.html
msgid ""
"The Maya of Central America used three separate, overlapping calendar "
"systems, the <em class=\"emph\">long count</em>, the <em "
"class=\"emph\">tzolkin</em>, and the <em class=\"emph\">haab</em>.  Emacs "
"knows about all three of these calendars.  Experts dispute the exact "
"correlation between the Mayan calendar and our calendar; Emacs uses the "
"Goodman-Martinez-Thompson correlation in its calculations."
msgstr ""
"中米のマヤ文明では、<em class=\"emph\">ロングカウント</em>、<em "
"class=\"emph\">ツォルキン</em>、<em class=\"emph\">ハアブ</em>という、互いに"
"重なり合う3つの独立した暦体系が用いられていました。Emacsはこれら3つの暦すべて"
"に対応しています。マヤ暦と現代の暦との正確な対応関係については専門家の間でも"
"見解が分かれていますが、Emacsは計算にGoodman-Martinez-Thompsonの対応関係を採"
"用しています。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/emacs/Calendar-Systems.html
msgid ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-Coptic-calendar\"></a> <a "
"class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-Ethiopic-calendar\"></a>"
msgstr ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-Coptic-calendar\"></a> <a "
"class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-Ethiopic-calendar\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Calendar-Systems.html
msgid ""
"The Copts use a calendar based on the ancient Egyptian solar calendar.  "
"Their calendar consists of twelve 30-day months followed by an extra five-"
"day period.  Once every fourth year they add a leap day to this extra period "
"to make it six days.  The Ethiopic calendar is identical in structure, but "
"has different year numbers and month names."
msgstr ""
"コプト教徒は、古代エジプトの太陽暦に基づく暦を用いている。その暦は30日からな"
"る12か月と、その後に続く5日間の追加期間で構成されている。4年に一度、この追加"
"期間に閏日を加えて6日間とする。エチオピア暦は構造こそ同一だが、年号と月名が異"
"なる。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/emacs/Calendar-Systems.html
msgid ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-Persian-calendar\"></a> <a "
"class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-Birashk\"></a>"
msgstr ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-Persian-calendar\"></a> <a "
"class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-Birashk\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Calendar-Systems.html
msgid ""
"The Persians use a solar calendar based on a design of Omar Khayyam.  Their "
"calendar consists of twelve months of which the first six have 31 days, the "
"next five have 30 days, and the last has 29 in ordinary years and 30 in leap "
"years.  Leap years occur in a complicated pattern every four or five years.  "
"The calendar implemented here is the arithmetical Persian calendar "
"championed by Birashk, based on a 2,820-year cycle.  It differs from the "
"astronomical Persian calendar, which is based on astronomical events.  As of "
"this writing the first future discrepancy is projected to occur on March 20, "
"2025.  It is currently not clear what the official calendar of Iran will be "
"at that time."
msgstr ""
"ペルシア人は、ウマル・ハイヤームの設計に基づく太陽暦を使用している。この暦は"
"12か月で構成されており、通常年では最初の6か月が31日、次の5か月が30日、そして"
"最後の1か月が29日または30日となっている。閏年は4年または5年ごとに複雑な周期で"
"訪れる。ここで採用されているのは、ビラシュクが提唱した2,820年周期に基づく算術"
"的ペルシア暦である。これは、天文現象に基づく天文学的ペルシア暦とは異なる。本"
"稿執筆時点で、最初のずれは2025年3月20日に発生すると予測されている。その時点で"
"のイランの公式暦がどうなるかは、現時点では明らかではない。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/emacs/Calendar-Systems.html
msgid "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-Chinese-calendar\"></a>"
msgstr "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-Chinese-calendar\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Calendar-Systems.html
msgid ""
"The Chinese calendar is a complicated system of lunar months arranged into "
"solar years.  The years go in cycles of sixty, each year containing either "
"twelve months in an ordinary year or thirteen months in a leap year; each "
"month has either 29 or 30 days.  Years, ordinary months, and days are named "
"by combining one of ten <em class=\"dfn\">celestial stems</em> with one of "
"twelve <em class=\"dfn\">terrestrial branches</em> for a total of sixty "
"names that are repeated in a cycle of sixty."
msgstr ""
"中国の暦は、太陰月を太陽年に組み込んだ複雑な体系である。年は60年周期で巡って"
"おり、平年は12か月、閏年は13か月で構成され、各月は29日または30日となる。年、"
"平月、および日は、10種類の<em class=\"dfn\">天干</em>と12種類の<em "
"class=\"dfn\">地支</em>のいずれかを組み合わせて命名され、計60種類の名称が60年"
"周期で繰り返される。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/emacs/Calendar-Systems.html
msgid "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-Baha_0027i-calendar\"></a>"
msgstr "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-Baha_0027i-calendar\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Calendar-Systems.html
msgid ""
"The Bah&aacute;&rsquo;&iacute; calendar system is based on a solar cycle of "
"19 months with 19 days each.  The remaining intercalary days (known as "
"Ayy&aacute;m-i-H&aacute;) are placed between the 18th and 19th months.  "
"Following a 2014 calendar reform by the Universal House of Justice, the date "
"of Naw-R&uacute;z (New Year) is now determined by the vernal equinox as "
"observed from Tehran, and the dates of the Twin Holy Birthdays (Birth of the "
"B&aacute;b and Birth of Bah&aacute;&rsquo;u&rsquo;ll&aacute;h) are "
"calculated from the eighth new moon after Naw-R&uacute;z.  For dates before "
"172 BE (2015 CE), the calendar follows the pre-reform fixed calculations."
msgstr ""
"バハーイー暦は、各月19日からなる19か月の太陽周期に基づいています。残りの閏日"
"（アーヤム・イ・ハーとして知られる）は、第18月と第19月の間に配置されます。万"
"国正義院による2014年の暦改革以降、ナウルーズ（新年）の日付はテヘランで観測さ"
"れる春分点によって決定され、二つの聖なる誕生日（バブの誕生およびバハーウッ"
"ラーの誕生）の日付は、ナウルーズ後の8回目の新月から算出されます。紀元前172年"
"（西暦2015年）より前の日付については、暦は改革前の固定計算に従っています。"

