# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Compilation-Mode.html
msgid ""
"If you change the variable <code class=\"code\">compilation-auto-jump-to-"
"first-error</code> to a non-<code class=\"code\">nil</code> value, Emacs "
"automatically visits the locus of the first error message that appears in "
"the <samp class=\"file\">*compilation*</samp> buffer.  (This variable can "
"also have the values <code class=\"code\">if-location-known</code> and <code "
"class=\"code\">first-known</code>, which modify the conditions for "
"automatically visiting the error locus.)"
msgstr ""
"変数 <code class=\"code\">compilation-auto-jump-to-first-error</code> を "
"<code class=\"code\">nil</code> 以外の値に変更すると、Emacs は <samp "
"class=\"file\">*compilation*</samp> バッファに最初に現れたエラーメッセージの"
"箇所に自動的に移動します。（この変数には <code class=\"code\">if-location-"
"known</code> や <code class=\"code\">first-known</code> という値も指定でき、"
"これによりエラー箇所へ自動的に移動する条件を変更できます。）"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/emacs/Compilation-Mode.html
msgid ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-compilation_002dsearch_002dpath\"></"
"a> <a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-"
"compilation_002dsearch_002dextra_002dpath\"></a>"
msgstr ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-compilation_002dsearch_002dpath\"></"
"a> <a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-"
"compilation_002dsearch_002dextra_002dpath\"></a>"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Compilation-Mode.html
msgid ""
"The actual locus of an error message is determined by <code "
"class=\"code\">compilation-search-path</code>, a list of directory names.  "
"By default, Emacs visits the file indicated in the error message under the "
"directory where the compilation happens, represented by the special "
"directory name <code class=\"code\">nil</code> in the default value for "
"<code class=\"code\">compilation-search-path</code> (i.e. <code "
"class=\"code\">(nil)</code>).  To make Emacs try to find the file under a "
"different directory (e.g. when compiling a nested project), customize <code "
"class=\"code\">compilation-search-path</code> to include that directory.  "
"For directory-local customization (see <a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Directory-"
"Variables.html\">Per-Directory Local Variables</a>), prefer setting <code "
"class=\"code\">compilation-search-extra-path</code> instead, which Emacs "
"considers in addition to <code class=\"code\">compilation-search-path</"
"code>.  Entries in <code class=\"code\">compilation-search-extra-path</code> "
"take precedence over entries in <code class=\"code\">compilation-search-"
"path</code>."
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
