"entry-id\" id=\"index-add_002dmode_002dabbrev\"></a>"
msgstr ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-C_002dx-a-l\"></a> <a class=\"index-"
"entry-id\" id=\"index-add_002dmode_002dabbrev\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Defining-Abbrevs.html
msgid ""
"The command <kbd class=\"kbd\">C-x a l</kbd> (<code class=\"code\">add-mode-"
"abbrev</code>) is similar, but defines a mode-specific abbrev for the "
"current major mode.  The arguments work the same as for <kbd class=\"kbd\">C-"
"x a g</kbd>."
msgstr ""
"コマンド <kbd class=\"kbd\">C-x a l</kbd> (<code class=\"code\">add-mode-"
"abbrev</code>) も同様ですが、現在のメジャーモード専用の略記を定義します。引数"
"の扱いは <kbd class=\"kbd\">C-x a g</kbd> と同じです。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/emacs/Defining-Abbrevs.html
msgid ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-C_002dx-a-i-g\"></a> <a class=\"index-"
"entry-id\" id=\"index-inverse_002dadd_002dglobal_002dabbrev\"></a> <a "
"class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-C_002dx-a-i-l\"></a> <a class=\"index-"
"entry-id\" id=\"index-inverse_002dadd_002dmode_002dabbrev\"></a>"
msgstr ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-C_002dx-a-i-g\"></a> <a class=\"index-"
"entry-id\" id=\"index-inverse_002dadd_002dglobal_002dabbrev\"></a> <a "
"class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-C_002dx-a-i-l\"></a> <a class=\"index-"
"entry-id\" id=\"index-inverse_002dadd_002dmode_002dabbrev\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Defining-Abbrevs.html
msgid ""
"<kbd class=\"kbd\">C-x a i g</kbd> (<code class=\"code\">inverse-add-global-"
"abbrev</code>) and <kbd class=\"kbd\">C-x a i l</kbd> (<code "
"class=\"code\">inverse-add-mode-abbrev</code>) perform the opposite task: if "
"the abbrev text is already in the buffer, you use these commands to define "
"an abbrev by specifying the expansion in the minibuffer.  These commands "
"will expand the abbrev text used for the definition."
msgstr ""
"<kbd class=\"kbd\">C-x a i g</kbd> (<code class=\"code\">inverse-add-global-"
"abbrev</code>) および <kbd class=\"kbd\">C-x a i l</kbd> (<code "
"class=\"code\">inverse-add-mode-abbrev</code>) は逆の処理を行います。略語テキ"
"ストが既にバッファにある場合、これらのコマンドを使用して、ミニバッファで展開"
"内容を指定し、略語を定義します。これらのコマンドは、定義に使用された略語テキ"
"ストを展開します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/emacs/Defining-Abbrevs.html
msgid ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-define_002dmode_002dabbrev\"></a> <a "
"class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-define_002dglobal_002dabbrev\"></a>"
msgstr ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-define_002dmode_002dabbrev\"></a> <a "
"class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-define_002dglobal_002dabbrev\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Defining-Abbrevs.html
msgid ""
"You can define an abbrev without inserting either the abbrev or its "
"expansion in the buffer using the command <code class=\"code\">define-global-"
"abbrev</code>.  It reads two arguments&mdash;the abbrev, and its expansion.  "
"The command <code class=\"code\">define-mode-abbrev</code> does likewise for "
"a mode-specific abbrev."
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">define-global-abbrev</code> コマンドを使用すると、バッ"
"ファ内に略語やその展開形を挿入することなく、略語を定義できます。このコマンド"
"は、略語とその展開形という2つの引数を受け取ります。<code "
"class=\"code\">define-mode-abbrev</code> コマンドも同様に、モード固有の略語に"
"対して機能します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Defining-Abbrevs.html
msgid ""
"To change the definition of an abbrev, just make a new definition.  When an "
"abbrev has a prior definition, the abbrev definition commands ask for "
"confirmation before replacing it."
msgstr ""
"略語の定義を変更するには、新たに定義を作成してください。略語に既存の定義があ"
"る場合、略語定義コマンドは置き換える前に確認を求めます。"

