#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><h4>
#: build/html/emacs/ForIndent-Conv.html
msgid ""
"<span>28.14.2.4 Syntactic Conventions<a class=\"copiable-link\" "
"href=\"#Syntactic-Conventions\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span>28.14.2.4 構文上の規約<a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#Syntactic-"
"Conventions\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/emacs/ForIndent-Conv.html
msgid ""
"Fortran mode assumes that you follow certain conventions that simplify the "
"task of understanding a Fortran program well enough to indent it properly:"
msgstr ""
"Fortranモードでは、Fortranプログラムを十分に理解して適切にインデントできるよ"
"う、特定の規約に従うことを前提としています："

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li>
#: build/html/emacs/ForIndent-Conv.html
msgid ""
"Two nested &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">do</samp>&rsquo; loops never share a "
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">continue</samp>&rsquo; statement."
msgstr ""
"入れ子になった2つの&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">do</samp>&rsquo;ループが、"
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">continue</samp>&rsquo;文を共有することはありませ"
"ん。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li>
#: build/html/emacs/ForIndent-Conv.html
msgid ""
"Fortran keywords such as &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">if</samp>&rsquo;, "
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">else</samp>&rsquo;, &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">then</samp>&rsquo;, &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">do</"
"samp>&rsquo; and others are written without embedded whitespace or line "
"breaks."
msgstr ""
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">if</samp>&rsquo;、&lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">else</samp>&rsquo;、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">then</"
"samp>&rsquo;、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">do</samp>&rsquo;などのFortranキー"
"ワードは、埋め込まれた空白や改行なしで記述されます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li><p>
#: build/html/emacs/ForIndent-Conv.html
msgid ""
"Fortran compilers generally ignore whitespace outside of string constants, "
"but Fortran mode does not recognize these keywords if they are not "
"contiguous.  Constructs such as &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">else if</"
"samp>&rsquo; or &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">end do</samp>&rsquo; are "
"acceptable, but the second word should be on the same line as the first and "
"not on a continuation line."
msgstr ""
"Fortranコンパイラは一般に、文字列定数以外の空白を無視しますが、Fortranモード"
"では、これらのキーワードが連続していない場合は認識されません。&lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">else if</samp>&rsquo; や &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">end do</"
"samp>&rsquo; のような記述は許容されますが、2番目の単語は1番目の単語と同じ行に"
"記述する必要があり、継続行に記述してはなりません。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/emacs/ForIndent-Conv.html
msgid ""
"If you fail to follow these conventions, the indentation commands may indent "
"some lines unaesthetically.  However, a correct Fortran program retains its "
"meaning when reindented even if the conventions are not followed."
msgstr ""
"これらの規約に従わない場合、インデントコマンドによって一部の行が不自然にイン"
"デントされることがあります。ただし、正しいFortranプログラムであれば、規約に"
"従っていない場合でも、再インデントしてもその意味は維持されます。"

