"<a class=\"xref\" href=\"#Glossary_002d_002d_002dEnd-Of-Line\">用語集---行末"
"</a>を参照してください。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/emacs/Glossary.html
msgid "Error"
msgstr "エラー"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Glossary.html
msgid ""
"An error occurs when an Emacs command cannot execute in the current "
"circumstances.  When an error occurs, execution of the command stops (unless "
"the command has been programmed to do otherwise) and Emacs reports the error "
"by displaying an error message (q.v.)."
msgstr ""
"現在の状況でEmacsコマンドが実行できない場合、エラーが発生します。エラーが発生"
"すると、コマンドの実行は停止し（別途そのようにプログラムされていない限り）、"
"Emacsはエラーメッセージ（参照）を表示してエラーを報告します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/emacs/Glossary.html
msgid "Error Message"
msgstr "エラーメッセージ"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Glossary.html
msgid ""
"An error message is output displayed by Emacs when you ask it to do "
"something impossible (such as, killing text forward when point is at the end "
"of the buffer), or when a command malfunctions in some way.  Such messages "
"appear in the echo area, accompanied by a beep."
msgstr ""
"Emacsに不可能な操作（例えば、ポイントがバッファの末尾にある状態で前方のテキス"
"トを消去するなど）を指示した場合や、コマンドが何らかの形で正常に動作しなかっ"
"た場合に、エラーメッセージが出力されます。こうしたメッセージは、ビープ音とと"
"もにエコーエリアに表示されます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/emacs/Glossary.html
msgid "<kbd class=\"key\">ESC</kbd>"
msgstr "<kbd class=\"key\">ESC</kbd>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Glossary.html
msgid ""
"<kbd class=\"key\">ESC</kbd> is a character used as a prefix for typing Meta "
"characters on keyboards lacking a <kbd class=\"key\">Meta</kbd> key.  Unlike "
"the <kbd class=\"key\">Meta</kbd> key (which, like the <kbd "
"class=\"key\">SHIFT</kbd> key, is held down while another character is "
"typed), you press the <kbd class=\"key\">ESC</kbd> key as you would press a "
"letter key, and it applies to the next character you type."
msgstr ""
"<kbd class=\"key\">ESC</kbd> は、<kbd class=\"key\">Meta</kbd> キーのないキー"
"ボードでメタ文字を入力する際に接頭辞として使用される文字です。<kbd "
"class=\"key\">Meta</kbd> キー（<kbd class=\"key\">SHIFT</kbd> キーと同様に、"
"別の文字を入力する際に押し続けるもの）とは異なり、<kbd class=\"key\">ESC</"
"kbd> キーはアルファベットキーを押すのと同じように入力し、次に入力する文字に適"
"用されます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/emacs/Glossary.html
msgid "etc."
msgstr "など。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Glossary.html
msgid ""
"Short for &ldquo;et cetera&rdquo; in Latin, which means &ldquo;and so "
"on&rdquo;."
msgstr "ラテン語の「et cetera」の略で、「などなど」という意味。"

