#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><h4>
#: build/html/emacs/Hooks.html
msgid ""
"<span>51.2.2 Hooks<a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#Hooks-1\"> &para;</a></"
"span>"
msgstr ""
"<span>51.2.2 フック<a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#Hooks-1\"> &para;</a></"
"span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/emacs/Hooks.html
msgid ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-hook\"></a> <a class=\"index-entry-"
"id\" id=\"index-running-a-hook\"></a>"
msgstr ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-hook\"></a> <a class=\"index-entry-"
"id\" id=\"index-running-a-hook\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Hooks.html
msgid ""
"<em class=\"dfn\">Hooks</em> are an important mechanism for customizing "
"Emacs.  A hook is a Lisp variable which holds a list of functions, to be "
"called on some well-defined occasion.  (This is called <em "
"class=\"dfn\">running the hook</em>.)  The individual functions in the list "
"are called the <em class=\"dfn\">hook functions</em> of the hook.  For "
"example, the hook <code class=\"code\">kill-emacs-hook</code> runs just "
"before exiting Emacs (see <a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Exiting.html\">Exiting "
"Emacs</a>)."
msgstr ""
"<em class=\"dfn\">フック</em>は、Emacsをカスタマイズするための重要な仕組みで"
"す。フックとは、明確に定義されたタイミングで呼び出される関数のリストを保持す"
"るLisp変数のことです。（これを<em class=\"dfn\">フックを実行する</em>と呼びま"
"す。）リストに含まれる個々の関数は、そのフックの<em class=\"dfn\">フック関数"
"</em>と呼ばれます。例えば、フック <code class=\"code\">kill-emacs-hook</"
"code> はEmacsを終了する直前に実行されます（<a class=\"pxref\" "
"href=\"Exiting.html\">Emacsの終了</a>を参照）。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/emacs/Hooks.html
msgid "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-normal-hook\"></a>"
msgstr "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-normal-hook\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Hooks.html
msgid ""
"Most hooks are <em class=\"dfn\">normal hooks</em>.  This means that when "
"Emacs runs the hook, it calls each hook function in turn, with no "
"arguments.  We have made an effort to keep most hooks normal, so that you "
"can use them in a uniform way.  Every variable whose name ends in &lsquo;"
"<samp class=\"samp\">-hook</samp>&rsquo; is a normal hook."
msgstr ""
"ほとんどのフックは<em class=\"dfn\">通常のフック</em>です。つまり、Emacsが"
"フックを実行する際、各フック関数を引数なしで順に呼び出します。ほとんどのフッ"
"クを通常のフックにすることで、統一的な方法で利用できるよう配慮しています。名"
"前が&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">-hook</samp>&rsquo;で終わる変数はすべて通常の"
"フックです。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/emacs/Hooks.html
msgid "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-abnormal-hook\"></a>"
msgstr "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-abnormal-hook\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Hooks.html
msgid ""
"A few hooks are <em class=\"dfn\">abnormal hooks</em>.  Their names end in "
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">-functions</samp>&rsquo;, instead of &lsquo;"
"<samp class=\"samp\">-hook</samp>&rsquo; (some old code may also use the "
"deprecated suffix &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">-hooks</samp>&rsquo;).  What "
"makes these hooks abnormal is the way its functions are called&mdash;perhaps "
"they are given arguments, or perhaps the values they return are used in some "
"way.  For example, <code class=\"code\">find-file-not-found-functions</code> "
"is abnormal because as soon as one hook function returns a non-<code "
"class=\"code\">nil</code> value, the rest are not called at all (see <a "
"class=\"pxref\" href=\"Visiting.html\">Visiting Files</a>).  The "
"documentation of each abnormal hook variable explains how its functions are "
"used."
msgstr ""
"一部のフックは<em class=\"dfn\">異常フック</em>です。その名称は、<samp "
"class=\"samp\">-hook</samp>ではなく&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">-functions</"
"samp>&rsquo;で終わります（古いコードの中には、非推奨の接尾辞&lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">-hooks</samp>&rsquo;を使用しているものもあります）。これらの"
"フックが異常とされる理由は、その関数の呼び出し方にあります。例えば、引数が渡"
"されていたり、戻り値が何らかの形で利用されていたりする場合などです。具体例を"
"挙げると、<code class=\"code\">find-file-not-found-functions</code>が異常なの"
"は、いずれか一つのフック関数が<code class=\"code\">nil</code>以外の値を返す"
"と、残りの関数は一切呼び出されないためです（<a class=\"pxref\" "
"href=\"Visiting.html\">ファイルの参照</a>を参照）。各異常フック変数のドキュメ"
"ントには、その関数がどのように使用されるかが説明されています。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/emacs/Hooks.html
msgid "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-add_002dhook\"></a>"
msgstr "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-add_002dhook\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Hooks.html
msgid ""
"You can set a hook variable with <code class=\"code\">setq</code> like any "
"other Lisp variable, but the recommended way to add a function to a hook "
"(either normal or abnormal) is to use <code class=\"code\">add-hook</code>, "
"as shown by the following examples.  See <a data-manual=\"elisp\" "
"href=\"https://www.gnu.org/software/emacs/manual/html_node/elisp/"
"Hooks.html#Hooks\">Hooks</a> in <cite class=\"cite\">The Emacs Lisp "
"Reference Manual</cite>, for details."
msgstr ""
"他のLisp変数と同様に、<code class=\"code\">setq</code> でフック変数を設定でき"
"ますが、フック（通常または異常）に関数を追加する推奨方法は、以下の例に示すよ"
"うに <code class=\"code\">add-hook</code> を使用することです。詳細について"
"は、<cite class=\"cite\">The Emacs Lisp Reference Manual</cite> の <a data-"
"manual=\"elisp\" href=\"https://www.gnu.org/software/emacs/manual/html_node/"
"elisp/Hooks.html#Hooks\">Hooks</a> を参照してください。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Hooks.html
msgid ""
"Most major modes run one or more <em class=\"dfn\">mode hooks</em> as the "
"last step of initialization.  Mode hooks are a convenient way to customize "
"the behavior of individual modes; they are always normal.  For example, "
"here&rsquo;s how to set up a hook to turn on Auto Fill mode in Text mode and "
"other modes based on Text mode:"
msgstr ""
"ほとんどの主要なモードでは、初期化の最終ステップとして1つ以上の<em "
"class=\"dfn\">モードフック</em>が実行されます。モードフックは、個々のモードの"
"動作をカスタマイズするための便利な手段であり、常に通常モードで動作します。例"
"えば、テキストモードおよびテキストモードをベースとしたその他のモードでオート"
"フィルモードを有効にするフックを設定する方法は以下の通りです。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li><div><pre>
#: build/html/emacs/Hooks.html build/html/emacs/Init-Examples.html
#, no-wrap
msgid "(add-hook 'text-mode-hook 'auto-fill-mode)\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Hooks.html
msgid ""
"This works by calling <code class=\"code\">auto-fill-mode</code>, which "
"enables the minor mode when no argument is supplied (see <a class=\"pxref\" "
"href=\"Minor-Modes.html\">Minor Modes</a>).  Next, suppose you don&rsquo;t "
"want Auto Fill mode turned on in LaTeX mode, which is one of the modes based "
"on Text mode.  You can do this with the following additional line:"
msgstr ""
"これは <code class=\"code\">auto-fill-mode</code> を呼び出すことで動作し、引"
"数が指定されない場合にマイナーモードが有効になります（<a class=\"pxref\" "
"href=\"Minor-Modes.html\">マイナーモード</a> を参照）。次に、テキストモードに"
"基づくモードの一つである LaTeX モードにおいて、オートフィルモードを有効にした"
"くない場合を考えてみましょう。これは、以下の行を追加することで実現できます："

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><pre>
#: build/html/emacs/Hooks.html
#, no-wrap
msgid "(add-hook 'latex-mode-hook (lambda () (auto-fill-mode -1)))\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Hooks.html
msgid ""
"Here we have used the special macro <code class=\"code\">lambda</code> to "
"construct an anonymous function (see <a data-manual=\"elisp\" href=\"https://"
"www.gnu.org/software/emacs/manual/html_node/elisp/Lambda-"
"Expressions.html#Lambda-Expressions\">Lambda Expressions</a> in <cite "
"class=\"cite\">The Emacs Lisp Reference Manual</cite>), which calls <code "
"class=\"code\">auto-fill-mode</code> with an argument of <code "
"class=\"code\">-1</code> to disable the minor mode.  Because LaTeX mode runs "
"<code class=\"code\">latex-mode-hook</code> after running <code "
"class=\"code\">text-mode-hook</code>, the result leaves Auto Fill mode "
"disabled."
msgstr ""
"ここでは、特殊なマクロ <code class=\"code\">lambda</code> を用いて無名関数"
"（<cite class=\"cite\">The Emacs Lisp Reference Manual</cite> の <a data-"
"manual=\"elisp\" href=\"https://www.gnu.org/software/emacs/manual/html_node/"
"elisp/Lambda-Expressions.html#Lambda-Expressions\">Lambda Expressions</a> を"
"参照）を構築しており、これが <code class=\"code\">-1</code> を引数として "
"<code class=\"code\">auto-fill-mode</code> を呼び出すことでマイナーモードを無"
"効にします。LaTeX モードでは <code class=\"code\">text-mode-hook</code> の実"
"行後に <code class=\"code\">latex-mode-hook</code> が実行されるため、結果とし"
"て Auto Fill モードは無効なままとなります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Hooks.html
msgid ""
"Here is a more complex example, showing how to use a hook to customize the "
"indentation of C code:"
msgstr ""
"以下に、フックを使ってCコードのインデントをカスタマイズする方法を示す、より複"
"雑な例を挙げます。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/emacs/Hooks.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(setq my-c-style\n"
"  '((c-comment-only-line-offset . 4)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/emacs/Hooks.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    (c-cleanup-list . (scope-operator\n"
"                       empty-defun-braces\n"
"                       defun-close-semi))))\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/emacs/Hooks.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(add-hook 'c-mode-common-hook\n"
"  (lambda () (c-add-style &quot;my-style&quot; my-c-style t)))\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/emacs/Hooks.html
msgid ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-Prog-mode\"></a> <a class=\"index-"
"entry-id\" id=\"index-modes-for-editing-programs\"></a>"
msgstr ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-Prog-mode\"></a> <a class=\"index-"
"entry-id\" id=\"index-modes-for-editing-programs\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Hooks.html
msgid ""
"Major mode hooks also apply to other major modes <em class=\"dfn\">derived</"
"em> from the original mode (see <a data-manual=\"elisp\" href=\"https://"
"www.gnu.org/software/emacs/manual/html_node/elisp/Derived-Modes.html#Derived-"
"Modes\">Derived Modes</a> in <cite class=\"cite\">The Emacs Lisp Reference "
"Manual</cite>).  For instance, HTML mode is derived from Text mode (see <a "
"class=\"pxref\" href=\"HTML-Mode.html\">SGML and HTML Modes</a>); when HTML "
"mode is enabled, it runs <code class=\"code\">text-mode-hook</code> before "
"running <code class=\"code\">html-mode-hook</code>.  This provides a "
"convenient way to use a single hook to affect several related modes.  In "
"particular, if you want to apply a hook function to any programming language "
"mode, add it to <code class=\"code\">prog-mode-hook</code>; Prog mode is a "
"major mode that does little else than to let other major modes inherit from "
"it, exactly for this purpose."
msgstr ""
"メジャーモードのフックは、元のモードから<em class=\"dfn\">派生</em>した他のメ"
"ジャーモードにも適用されます（<cite class=\"cite\">The Emacs Lisp Reference "
"Manual</cite>の<a data-manual=\"elisp\" href=\"https://www.gnu.org/software/"
"emacs/manual/html_node/elisp/Derived-Modes.html#Derived-Modes\">Derived "
"Modes</a>を参照）。例えば、HTMLモードはTextモードから派生しています（<a "
"class=\"pxref\" href=\"HTML-Mode.html\">SGML and HTML Modes</a>を参照）。HTML"
"モードが有効な場合、<code class=\"code\">html-mode-hook</code>を実行する前に"
"<code class=\"code\">text-mode-hook</code>が実行されます。これにより、単一の"
"フックを用いて関連する複数のモードに影響を与えるという便利な方法が提供されま"
"す。特に、任意のプログラミング言語モードにフック関数を適用したい場合は、それ"
"を<code class=\"code\">prog-mode-hook</code>に追加してください。Progモード"
"は、まさにこの目的のために、他のメジャーモードが自身を継承できるようにするだ"
"けのメジャーモードです。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Hooks.html
msgid ""
"It is best to design your hook functions so that the order in which they are "
"executed does not matter.  Any dependence on the order is asking for "
"trouble.  However, the order is predictable: the hook functions are executed "
"in the order they appear in the hook."
msgstr ""
"フック関数は、実行順序に依存しないように設計するのが最善です。順序への依存は"
"トラブルの元となります。ただし、順序は予測可能です。フック関数は、フック内に"
"現れる順に実行されます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/emacs/Hooks.html
msgid "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-remove_002dhook\"></a>"
msgstr "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-remove_002dhook\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Hooks.html
msgid ""
"If you play with adding various different versions of a hook function by "
"calling <code class=\"code\">add-hook</code> over and over, remember that "
"all the versions you added will remain in the hook variable together.  You "
"can clear out individual functions by calling <code class=\"code\">remove-"
"hook</code>, or do <code class=\"code\">(setq <var class=\"var\">hook-"
"variable</var> nil)</code> to remove everything."
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">add-hook</code> を繰り返し呼び出してフック関数のさまざま"
"なバージョンを追加していく場合、追加したすべてのバージョンがフック変数に一括"
"して保持される点に注意してください。<code class=\"code\">remove-hook</code> "
"を呼び出して個別の関数をクリアしたり、<code class=\"code\">(setq <var "
"class=\"var\">hook-variable</var> nil)</code> を呼び出してすべてを削除したり"
"できます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/emacs/Hooks.html
msgid "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-buffer_002dlocal-hooks\"></a>"
msgstr "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-buffer_002dlocal-hooks\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Hooks.html
msgid ""
"If the hook variable is buffer-local, the buffer-local variable will be used "
"instead of the global variable.  However, if the buffer-local variable "
"contains the element <code class=\"code\">t</code>, the global hook variable "
"will be run as well."
msgstr ""
"hook変数がバッファローカルな場合、グローバル変数の代わりにバッファローカル変"
"数が使用されます。ただし、バッファローカル変数に要素 <code class=\"code\">t</"
"code> が含まれている場合は、グローバルのhook変数も実行されます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><hr><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Hooks.html
msgid ""
"<span class=\"nav-button\"><span class=\"nav-label\">Next: </span><span "
"class=\"nav-link\"><a href=\"Locals.html\">Local Variables</a></span></"
"span>, <span class=\"nav-button\"><span class=\"nav-label\">Previous: </"
"span><span class=\"nav-link\"><a href=\"Examining.html\">Examining and "
"Setting Variables</a></span></span>, <span class=\"nav-button\"><span "
"class=\"nav-label\">Up: </span><span class=\"nav-link\"><a "
