"a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<a id=\"index-batch-mode\"></a><span>&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">-batch</"
"samp>&rsquo;<a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-batch-mode\"> &para;</"
"a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd>
#: build/html/emacs/Initial-Options.html
msgid "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-_002d_002dbatch\"></a>"
msgstr "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-_002d_002dbatch\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/emacs/Initial-Options.html
msgid "&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">--batch</samp>&rsquo;"
msgstr "&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">--batch</samp>&rsquo;"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Initial-Options.html
msgid ""
"Run Emacs in <em class=\"dfn\">batch mode</em>.  Batch mode is used for "
"running programs written in Emacs Lisp from shell scripts, makefiles, and so "
"on.  To invoke a Lisp program, use the &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">-batch</"
"samp>&rsquo; option in conjunction with one or more of &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">-l</samp>&rsquo;, &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">-f</"
"samp>&rsquo; or &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">--eval</samp>&rsquo; (see <a "
"class=\"pxref\" href=\"Action-Arguments.html\">Action Arguments</a>).  See "
"<a class=\"xref\" href=\"Command-Example.html\">Command Argument Example</"
"a>, for an example."
msgstr ""
"Emacsを<em class=\"dfn\">バッチモード</em>で実行します。バッチモードは、シェ"
"ルスクリプトやmakefileなどからEmacs Lispで記述されたプログラムを実行する際に"
"使用します。Lispプログラムを呼び出すには、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">-"
"batch</samp>&rsquo;オプションを、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">-l</"
"samp>&rsquo;、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">-f</samp>&rsquo;、または&lsquo;"
"<samp class=\"samp\">--eval</samp>&rsquo;のいずれか1つ以上と組み合わせて使用"
"します（<a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Action-Arguments.html\">アクション引数</a>"
"を参照）。例については、<a class=\"xref\" href=\"Command-Example.html\">コマ"
"ンド引数の例</a>を参照してください。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd>
#: build/html/emacs/Initial-Options.html
msgid ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-kill_002demacs_002don_002dsigint\"></"
"a>"
msgstr ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-kill_002demacs_002don_002dsigint\"></"
"a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Initial-Options.html
msgid ""
"In batch mode, Emacs does not display the text being edited, and the "
"standard terminal interrupt characters such as <kbd class=\"kbd\">C-z</kbd> "
"and <kbd class=\"kbd\">C-c</kbd> have their usual effect: for <kbd "
"class=\"kbd\">C-c</kbd> that effect is either to exit Emacs or to signal "
"<code class=\"code\">quit</code>, depending on the variable <code "
"class=\"code\">kill-emacs-on-sigint</code>."
msgstr ""
"バッチモードでは、Emacsは編集中のテキストを表示せず、<kbd class=\"kbd\">C-z</"
"kbd>や<kbd class=\"kbd\">C-c</kbd>といった標準的なターミナル割り込み文字は通"
"常通りの動作をします。<kbd class=\"kbd\">C-c</kbd>の場合、その効果は変数"
"<code class=\"code\">kill-emacs-on-sigint</code>に応じて、Emacsを終了させる"
"か、あるいは<code class=\"code\">quit</code>にシグナルを送るかのいずれかにな"
"ります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Initial-Options.html
msgid ""
"Emacs functions that normally print a message in the echo area will print to "
"either the standard output stream (<code class=\"code\">stdout</code>) or "
"the standard error stream (<code class=\"code\">stderr</code>)  instead.  "
"(To be precise, functions like <code class=\"code\">prin1</code>, <code "
"class=\"code\">princ</code> and <code class=\"code\">print</code> print to "
"<code class=\"code\">stdout</code>, while <code class=\"code\">message</"
"code> and <code class=\"code\">error</code> print to <code "
"class=\"code\">stderr</code>.)  Functions that normally read keyboard input "
"from the minibuffer take their input from the terminal&rsquo;s standard "
"input stream (<code class=\"code\">stdin</code>) instead."
msgstr ""
"通常はエコーエリアにメッセージを出力するEmacs関数は、代わりに標準出力ストリー"
"ム (<code class=\"code\">stdout</code>) または標準エラーストリーム (<code "
"class=\"code\">stderr</code>) に出力します。（正確には、<code "
"class=\"code\">prin1</code>、<code class=\"code\">princ</code>、<code "
"class=\"code\">print</code> などの関数は <code class=\"code\">stdout</code> "
"に、<code class=\"code\">message</code> と <code class=\"code\">error</code> "
"は <code class=\"code\">stderr</code> に出力します。）通常はミニバッファから"
"キーボード入力を読み取る関数は、代わりにターミナルの標準入力ストリーム "
"(<code class=\"code\">stdin</code>) から入力を取得します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Initial-Options.html
msgid ""
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">--batch</samp>&rsquo; implies &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">-q</samp>&rsquo; (do not load an initialization file), but "
"<samp class=\"file\">site-start.el</samp> is loaded nonetheless.  It also "
"causes Emacs to exit after processing all the command options.  In addition, "
"it disables auto-saving except in buffers for which auto-saving is "
"explicitly requested, and when saving files it omits the <code "
"class=\"code\">fsync</code> system call unless otherwise requested."
msgstr ""
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">--batch</samp>&rsquo;は&lsquo;<samp "
