msgstr ""
"<span>I.12.1 MS-DOSでのキーボード操作<a class=\"copiable-link\" "
"href=\"#Keyboard-Usage-on-MS_002dDOS\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/emacs/MS_002dDOS-Keyboard.html
msgid ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-DEL-_0028MS_002dDOS_0029\"></a> <a "
"class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-BS-_0028MS_002dDOS_0029\"></a>"
msgstr ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-DEL-_0028MS_002dDOS_0029\"></a> <a "
"class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-BS-_0028MS_002dDOS_0029\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/emacs/MS_002dDOS-Keyboard.html
msgid ""
"The key that is called <kbd class=\"key\">DEL</kbd> in Emacs (because "
"that&rsquo;s how it is designated on most workstations) is known as <kbd "
"class=\"key\">BS</kbd> (backspace) on a PC.  That is why the PC-specific "
"terminal initialization remaps the <kbd class=\"key\">BS</kbd> key to act as "
"<kbd class=\"key\">DEL</kbd>; the <kbd class=\"key\">Delete</kbd> key is "
"remapped to act as <kbd class=\"kbd\">C-d</kbd> for the same reasons."
msgstr ""
"Emacsで<kbd class=\"key\">DEL</kbd>と呼ばれるキー（ほとんどのワークステーショ"
"ンでそのように指定されているため）は、PCでは<kbd class=\"key\">BS</kbd>（バッ"
"クスペース）として知られています。そのため、PC固有のターミナル初期化では<kbd "
"class=\"key\">BS</kbd>キーを<kbd class=\"key\">DEL</kbd>として動作するように"
"再マッピングしており、同様の理由で<kbd class=\"key\">Delete</kbd>キーも<kbd "
"class=\"kbd\">C-d</kbd>として動作するように再マッピングされています。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/emacs/MS_002dDOS-Keyboard.html
msgid ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-C_002dg-_0028MS_002dDOS_0029\"></a> "
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-C_002dBreak-_0028MS_002dDOS_0029\"></"
"a> <a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-quitting-on-MS_002dDOS\"></a>"
msgstr ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-C_002dg-_0028MS_002dDOS_0029\"></a> "
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-C_002dBreak-_0028MS_002dDOS_0029\"></"
"a> <a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-quitting-on-MS_002dDOS\"></a>"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/emacs/MS_002dDOS-Keyboard.html
msgid ""
"Emacs built for MS-DOS recognizes <kbd class=\"kbd\">C-<kbd "
"class=\"key\">Break</kbd></kbd> as a quit character, just like <kbd "
"class=\"kbd\">C-g</kbd>.  This is because Emacs cannot detect that you have "
"typed <kbd class=\"kbd\">C-g</kbd> until it is ready for more input.  As a "
"consequence, you cannot use <kbd class=\"kbd\">C-g</kbd> to stop a running "
"command (see <a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Quitting.html\">Quitting and "
"Aborting</a>).  By contrast, <kbd class=\"kbd\">C-<kbd class=\"key\">Break</"
"kbd></kbd> <em class=\"emph\">is</em> detected as soon as you type it (as "
"<kbd class=\"kbd\">C-g</kbd> is on other systems), so it can be used to stop "
"a running command and for emergency escape (see <a class=\"pxref\" "
"href=\"Emergency-Escape.html\">Emergency Escape</a>)."
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/emacs/MS_002dDOS-Keyboard.html
msgid ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-Meta-_0028under-MS_002dDOS_0029\"></"
"a> <a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-Hyper-_0028under-"
"MS_002dDOS_0029\"></a> <a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-Super-"
"_0028under-MS_002dDOS_0029\"></a> <a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-"
"dos_002dsuper_002dkey\"></a> <a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-"
"dos_002dhyper_002dkey\"></a>"
msgstr ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-Meta-_0028under-MS_002dDOS_0029\"></"
"a> <a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-Hyper-_0028under-"
"MS_002dDOS_0029\"></a> <a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-Super-"
"_0028under-MS_002dDOS_0029\"></a> <a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-"
"dos_002dsuper_002dkey\"></a> <a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-"
"dos_002dhyper_002dkey\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/emacs/MS_002dDOS-Keyboard.html
msgid ""
"The PC keyboard maps use the left <kbd class=\"key\">Alt</kbd> key as the "
"<kbd class=\"key\">Meta</kbd> key.  You have two choices for emulating the "
"<kbd class=\"key\">SUPER</kbd> and <kbd class=\"key\">Hyper</kbd> keys: "
"choose either the right <kbd class=\"key\">Ctrl</kbd> key or the right <kbd "
"class=\"key\">Alt</kbd> key by setting the variables <code "
"class=\"code\">dos-hyper-key</code> and <code class=\"code\">dos-super-key</"
"code> to 1 or 2 respectively.  If neither <code class=\"code\">dos-super-"
"key</code> nor <code class=\"code\">dos-hyper-key</code> is 1, then by "
"default the right <kbd class=\"key\">Alt</kbd> key is also mapped to the "
"<kbd class=\"key\">Meta</kbd> key.  However, if the MS-DOS international "
"keyboard support program <samp class=\"file\">KEYB.COM</samp> is installed, "
"Emacs will <em class=\"emph\">not</em> map the right <kbd class=\"key\">Alt</"
"kbd> to <kbd class=\"key\">Meta</kbd>, since it is used for accessing "
"characters like <kbd class=\"kbd\">~</kbd> and <kbd class=\"kbd\">@</kbd> on "
"non-US keyboard layouts; in this case, you may only use the left <kbd "
"class=\"key\">Alt</kbd> as <kbd class=\"key\">Meta</kbd> key."
msgstr ""
"PCキーボードのマッピングでは、左の<kbd class=\"key\">Alt</kbd>キーが<kbd "
"class=\"key\">Meta</kbd>キーとして割り当てられています。<kbd "
"class=\"key\">SUPER</kbd>および<kbd class=\"key\">Hyper</kbd>キーをエミュレー"
"トするには、2つの選択肢があります。変数<code class=\"code\">dos-hyper-key</"
"code>と<code class=\"code\">dos-super-key</code>をそれぞれ1または2に設定する"
"ことで、右の<kbd class=\"key\">Ctrl</kbd>キーか右の<kbd class=\"key\">Alt</"
"kbd>キーのいずれかを選択できます。<code class=\"code\">dos-super-key</code>と"
"<code class=\"code\">dos-hyper-key</code>のどちらも1でない場合、デフォルトで"
"は右の<kbd class=\"key\">Alt</kbd>キーも<kbd class=\"key\">Meta</kbd>キーに"
"マッピングされます。ただし、MS-DOSの国際キーボードサポートプログラム<samp "
"class=\"file\">KEYB.COM</samp>がインストールされている場合、Emacsは右の<kbd "
"class=\"key\">Alt</kbd>キーを<kbd class=\"key\">Meta</kbd>にマッピング<em "
"class=\"emph\">しません</em>。これは、米国以外のキーボードレイアウトにおいて"
"<kbd class=\"kbd\">~</kbd>や<kbd class=\"kbd\">@</kbd>といった文字へのアクセ"
"スに使用されるためです。この場合、左の<kbd class=\"key\">Alt</kbd>キーを<kbd "
"class=\"key\">Meta</kbd>キーとして使用することしかできません。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/emacs/MS_002dDOS-Keyboard.html
msgid ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-C_002dj-_0028MS_002dDOS_0029\"></a> "
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-dos_002dkeypad_002dmode\"></a>"
msgstr ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-C_002dj-_0028MS_002dDOS_0029\"></a> "
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-dos_002dkeypad_002dmode\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/emacs/MS_002dDOS-Keyboard.html
msgid ""
"The variable <code class=\"code\">dos-keypad-mode</code> is a flag variable "
"that controls what key codes are returned by keys in the numeric keypad.  "
"You can also define the keypad <kbd class=\"key\">ENTER</kbd> key to act "
"like <kbd class=\"kbd\">C-j</kbd>, by putting the following line into your "
"<samp class=\"file\">_emacs</samp> file:"
msgstr ""
"変数 <code class=\"code\">dos-keypad-mode</code> は、テンキーのキーからどの"
"キーコードが返されるかを制御するフラグ変数です。また、<samp "
"class=\"file\">_emacs</samp> ファイルに以下の行を記述することで、テンキーの "
"<kbd class=\"key\">ENTER</kbd> キーを <kbd class=\"kbd\">C-j</kbd> と同様に動"
"作させるように定義することも可能です："

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><pre>
