# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Mail-Headers.html
msgid ""
"A header field in the mail buffer starts with a field name at the beginning "
"of a line, terminated by a colon.  Upper and lower case are equivalent in "
"field names.  After the colon and optional whitespace comes the contents of "
"the field."
msgstr ""
"メールバッファ内のヘッダーフィールドは、行頭のフィールド名で始まり、コロンで"
"終了します。フィールド名では大文字と小文字は区別されません。コロンと任意の空"
"白文字の後に、フィールドの内容が続きます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Mail-Headers.html
msgid ""
"You can use any name you like for a header field, but normally people use "
"only standard field names with accepted meanings."
msgstr ""
"ヘッダーフィールドには任意の名前を使用できますが、通常は一般的に認められてい"
"る意味を持つ標準的なフィールド名のみが使用されます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/emacs/Mail-Headers.html
msgid ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-user_002dfull_002dname\"></a> <a "
"class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-user_002dmail_002daddress\"></a>"
msgstr ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-user_002dfull_002dname\"></a> <a "
"class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-user_002dmail_002daddress\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Mail-Headers.html
msgid ""
"The &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">From</samp>&rsquo; header field identifies "
"the person sending the email (i.e., you).  This should be a valid mailing "
"address, as replies are normally sent there.  The default contents of this "
"header field are computed from the variables <code class=\"code\">user-full-"
"name</code> (which specifies your full name) and <code class=\"code\">user-"
"mail-address</code> (your email address).  On some operating systems, Emacs "
"initializes these two variables using environment variables (see <a "
"class=\"pxref\" href=\"General-Variables.html\">General Variables</a>).  If "
"this information is unavailable or wrong, you should customize the variables "
"yourself (see <a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Easy-Customization.html\">Easy "
"Customization Interface</a>)."
msgstr ""
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">From</samp>&rsquo; ヘッダーフィールドは、メールの"
"送信者（すなわちあなた）を識別します。返信は通常そこに送信されるため、有効な"
"メールアドレスである必要があります。このヘッダーフィールドのデフォルト内容"
"は、変数 <code class=\"code\">user-full-name</code>（フルネームを指定）と "
"<code class=\"code\">user-mail-address</code>（メールアドレス）から算出されま"
"す。一部のオペレーティングシステムでは、Emacs は環境変数を用いてこれら 2 つの"
"変数を初期化します（<a class=\"pxref\" href=\"General-Variables.html\">一般変"
"数</a>を参照）。この情報が利用できないか、あるいは誤っている場合は、ご自身で"
"変数をカスタマイズしてください（<a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Easy-"
"Customization.html\">簡易カスタマイズインターフェース</a>を参照）。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Mail-Headers.html
msgid ""
"Apart from &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">From</samp>&rsquo;, here is a table "
"of commonly-used fields:"
msgstr ""
"「<samp class=\"samp\">From</samp>」を除き、よく使われるフィールドの一覧を以"
"下に示します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/emacs/Mail-Headers.html
msgid "&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">To</samp>&rsquo;"
msgstr "&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">To</samp>&rsquo;"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Mail-Headers.html
msgid ""
"The mailing address(es) to which the message is addressed.  To list more "
"than one address, use commas to separate them."
msgstr ""
"メッセージの宛先となる郵送先住所です。複数の住所を記載する場合は、カンマで区"
"切ってください。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/emacs/Mail-Headers.html
msgid "&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">Subject</samp>&rsquo;"
msgstr "&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">Subject</samp>&rsquo;"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Mail-Headers.html
msgid "The subject of the message."
msgstr "メッセージの件名。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/emacs/Mail-Headers.html
msgid "&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">CC</samp>&rsquo;"
msgstr "&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">CC</samp>&rsquo;"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Mail-Headers.html
msgid ""
"Additional mailing address(es) to send the message to.  This is like &lsquo;"
"<samp class=\"samp\">To</samp>&rsquo;, except that these readers should not "
"regard the message as directed at them."
msgstr ""
"メッセージを送信する追加の郵送先アドレス。これは「<samp class=\"samp\">To</"
"samp>」のようなものですが、これらのリーダーはメッセージを自分宛てのものとみな"
"すべきではありません。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/emacs/Mail-Headers.html
msgid "&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">BCC</samp>&rsquo;"
msgstr "&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">BCC</samp>&rsquo;"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Mail-Headers.html
msgid ""
"Additional mailing address(es) to send the message to, which should not "
"appear in the header of the message actually sent.  &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">BCC</samp>&rsquo; stands for <em class=\"dfn\">blind carbon "
"copies</em>."
msgstr ""
"メッセージを送信するための追加の郵送先アドレス。実際に送信されるメッセージの"
"ヘッダーには表示されません。&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">BCC</samp>&rsquo;は"
"<em class=\"dfn\">ブラインドカーボンコピー</em>を表します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/emacs/Mail-Headers.html
msgid "&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">FCC</samp>&rsquo;"
msgstr "&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">FCC</samp>&rsquo;"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Mail-Headers.html
msgid ""
"The name of a file, to which a copy of the sent message should be appended.  "
"Emacs writes the message in mbox format, unless the file is in Babyl format "
"(used by Rmail before Emacs 23), in which case Emacs writes in Babyl "
"format.  If an Rmail buffer is visiting the file, Emacs updates it "
"accordingly.  To specify more than one file, use several &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">FCC</samp>&rsquo; fields, with one file name in each field."
msgstr ""
"送信メッセージのコピーを追記するファイルの名前。Emacsは、ファイルがBabyl形式"
"（Emacs 23より前のRmailで使用されていた形式）でない限り、メッセージをmbox形式"
"で書き込みます。Babyl形式の場合は、EmacsはBabyl形式で書き込みます。Rmailバッ"
"ファがそのファイルを参照している場合、Emacsはそれに応じてバッファを更新しま"
"す。複数のファイルを指定するには、複数の&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">FCC</"
"samp>&rsquo;フィールドを使用し、各フィールドにファイル名を1つずつ記述します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/emacs/Mail-Headers.html
msgid "&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">Reply-To</samp>&rsquo;"
msgstr "&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">Reply-To</samp>&rsquo;"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Mail-Headers.html
msgid ""
"An address to which replies should be sent, instead of &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">From</samp>&rsquo;.  This is used if, for some reason, your "
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">From</samp>&rsquo; address cannot receive "
"replies."
msgstr ""
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">From</samp>&rsquo;の代わりに返信を送信すべきアド"
"レス。何らかの理由で&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">From</samp>&rsquo;アドレスが"
"返信を受信できない場合に使用されます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/emacs/Mail-Headers.html
msgid "&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">Mail-Reply-To</samp>&rsquo;"
msgstr "&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">Mail-Reply-To</samp>&rsquo;"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Mail-Headers.html
msgid ""
"This field takes precedence over &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">Reply-To</"
"samp>&rsquo;.  It is used because some mailing lists set the &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">Reply-To</samp>&rsquo; field for their own purposes (a "
"somewhat controversial practice)."
msgstr ""
"このフィールドは &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">Reply-To</samp>&rsquo; よりも優"
"先されます。一部のメーリングリストが独自の目的で &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">Reply-To</samp>&rsquo; フィールドを設定しているためです（これ"
"は少々議論のある慣行です）。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/emacs/Mail-Headers.html
msgid "&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">Mail-Followup-To</samp>&rsquo;"
msgstr "&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">Mail-Followup-To</samp>&rsquo;"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Mail-Headers.html
msgid ""
"One of more address(es) to use as default recipient(s) for follow-up "
"messages.  This is typically used when you reply to a message from a mailing "
"list that you are subscribed to, and want replies to go to the list without "
"sending an extra copy to you."
msgstr ""
"フォローアップメッセージのデフォルト宛先として使用する1つ以上のアドレス。通"
"常、購読しているメーリングリストからのメッセージに返信する際、自分宛てに別途"
"コピーを送信せず、返信をリスト宛に送る場合に使用します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/emacs/Mail-Headers.html
msgid "&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">In-Reply-To</samp>&rsquo;"
msgstr "&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">In-Reply-To</samp>&rsquo;"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Mail-Headers.html
msgid ""
"An identifier for the message you are replying to.  Most mail readers use "
"this information to group related messages together.  Normally, this header "
"is filled in automatically when you reply to a message in any mail program "
"built into Emacs."
msgstr ""
"返信先のメッセージの識別子です。ほとんどのメールリーダーはこの情報を利用し"
"て、関連するメッセージをグループ化します。通常、Emacsに内蔵されているメールプ"
"ログラムでメッセージに返信すると、このヘッダーは自動的に入力されます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/emacs/Mail-Headers.html
msgid "&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">References</samp>&rsquo;"
msgstr "&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">References</samp>&rsquo;"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Mail-Headers.html
msgid ""
"Identifiers for previous related messages.  Like &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">In-Reply-To</samp>&rsquo;, this is normally filled in "
"automatically for you."
msgstr ""
"過去の関連メッセージの識別子です。「<samp class=\"samp\">In-Reply-To</samp>」"
"と同様に、通常は自動的に入力されます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Mail-Headers.html
msgid ""
"The &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">To</samp>&rsquo;, &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">CC</samp>&rsquo;, and &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">BCC</"
"samp>&rsquo; fields can appear any number of times, and each such header "
"field can contain multiple addresses, separated by commas.  This way, you "
"can specify any number of places to send the message.  These fields can also "
"have continuation lines: one or more lines starting with whitespace, "
"following the starting line of the field, are considered part of the field.  "
"Here&rsquo;s an example of a &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">To</samp>&rsquo; "
"field with a continuation line:"
msgstr ""
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">To</samp>&rsquo;、&lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">CC</samp>&rsquo;、および&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">BCC</"
"samp>&rsquo;フィールドは任意の回数出現でき、各ヘッダーフィールドにはカンマで"
"区切られた複数のアドレスを含めることができます。これにより、メッセージを送信"
"する宛先を任意の数だけ指定できます。また、これらのフィールドには継続行を設け"
"ることも可能です。フィールドの開始行に続く、空白文字で始まる1行以上の行は、そ"
"のフィールドの一部とみなされます。以下に、継続行を含む&lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">To</samp>&rsquo;フィールドの例を示します。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/emacs/Mail-Headers.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To: foo@example.net, this@example.net,\n"
"  bob@example.com\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/emacs/Mail-Headers.html
msgid ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-mail_002ddefault_002dheaders\"></a>"
msgstr ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-mail_002ddefault_002dheaders\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Mail-Headers.html
msgid ""
"You can direct Emacs to insert certain default headers into the mail buffer "
"by setting the variable <code class=\"code\">mail-default-headers</code> to "
"a string.  Then <kbd class=\"kbd\">C-x m</kbd> inserts this string into the "
"message headers.  For example, here is how to add a &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">Reply-To</samp>&rsquo; and &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">FCC</"
"samp>&rsquo; header to each message:"
msgstr ""
"変数 <code class=\"code\">mail-default-headers</code> に文字列を設定すること"
"で、メールバッファに特定のデフォルトヘッダーを挿入するように Emacs に指示でき"
"ます。すると、<kbd class=\"kbd\">C-x m</kbd> がこの文字列をメッセージヘッダー"
"に挿入します。例えば、各メッセージに &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">Reply-To</"
"samp>&rsquo; と &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">FCC</samp>&rsquo; のヘッダーを追"
"加する方法は以下の通りです。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><div><pre>
#: build/html/emacs/Mail-Headers.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(setq mail-default-headers\n"
"      &quot;Reply-To: foo@example.com\\nFCC: ~/Mail/sent&quot;)\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Mail-Headers.html
msgid ""
"If the default header fields are not appropriate for a particular message, "
"edit them as necessary before sending the message."
msgstr ""
"特定のメッセージに対してデフォルトのヘッダーフィールドが適切でない場合は、"
"メッセージを送信する前に必要に応じて編集してください。"

