msgstr "<kbd class=\"kbd\">C-x h</kbd>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Marking-Objects.html
msgid ""
"Move point to the beginning of the buffer, and set mark at the end (<code "
"class=\"code\">mark-whole-buffer</code>)."
msgstr ""
"ポイントをバッファの先頭に移動し、末尾にマークを設定する (<code "
"class=\"code\">mark-whole-buffer</code>)。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/emacs/Marking-Objects.html
msgid ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-M_002d_0040\"></a> <a class=\"index-"
"entry-id\" id=\"index-mark_002dword\"></a>"
msgstr ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-M_002d_0040\"></a> <a class=\"index-"
"entry-id\" id=\"index-mark_002dword\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Marking-Objects.html
msgid ""
"<kbd class=\"kbd\">M-@</kbd> (<code class=\"code\">mark-word</code>) sets "
"the mark at the end of the next word (see <a class=\"pxref\" "
"href=\"Words.html\">Words</a>, for information about words).  Repeated "
"invocations of this command extend the region by advancing the mark one word "
"at a time.  As an exception, if the mark is active and located before point, "
"<kbd class=\"kbd\">M-@</kbd> moves the mark backwards from its current "
"position one word at a time."
msgstr ""
"<kbd class=\"kbd\">M-@</kbd> (<code class=\"code\">mark-word</code>) は、次の"
"単語の末尾にマークを設定します（単語に関する情報については、<a "
"class=\"pxref\" href=\"Words.html\">Words</a> を参照してください）。このコマ"
"ンドを繰り返し実行すると、マークが1単語ずつ進むことでリージョンが拡張されま"
"す。例外として、マークがアクティブでポイントより前に位置している場合、<kbd "
"class=\"kbd\">M-@</kbd> はマークを現在の位置から1単語ずつ後方に移動させます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Marking-Objects.html
msgid ""
"This command also accepts a numeric argument <var class=\"var\">n</var>, "
"which tells it to advance the mark by <var class=\"var\">n</var> words.  A "
"negative argument &minus;<var class=\"var\">n</var> moves the mark back by "
"<var class=\"var\">n</var> words."
msgstr ""
"このコマンドは数値引数 <var class=\"var\">n</var> も受け付け、これによりマー"
"クを <var class=\"var\">n</var> 単語分進めます。負の引数 &minus;<var "
"class=\"var\">n</var> は、マークを <var class=\"var\">n</var> 単語分戻しま"
"す。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/emacs/Marking-Objects.html
msgid ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-C_002dM_002d_0040\"></a> <a "
"class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-mark_002dsexp\"></a>"
msgstr ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-C_002dM_002d_0040\"></a> <a "
"class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-mark_002dsexp\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Marking-Objects.html
msgid ""
"Similarly, <kbd class=\"kbd\">C-M-@</kbd> (<code class=\"code\">mark-sexp</"
"code>) puts the mark at the end of the next balanced expression (see <a "
"class=\"pxref\" href=\"Expressions.html\">Expressions with Balanced "
"Parentheses</a>).  Repeated invocations extend the region to subsequent "
"expressions, while positive or negative numeric arguments move the mark "
"forward or backward by the specified number of expressions."
msgstr ""
"同様に、<kbd class=\"kbd\">C-M-@</kbd> (<code class=\"code\">mark-sexp</"
"code>) はマークを次のバランスのとれた式の末尾に配置します（<a "
"class=\"pxref\" href=\"Expressions.html\">バランスのとれた括弧を用いた式</a>"
"を参照）。繰り返し呼び出すと領域が後続の式まで拡張され、正または負の数値引数"
"を指定すると、マークが指定された式数分だけ前方または後方に移動します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Marking-Objects.html
msgid ""
"The other commands in the above list set both point and mark, so as to "
"delimit an object in the buffer.  <kbd class=\"kbd\">M-h</kbd> (<code "
"class=\"code\">mark-paragraph</code>)  marks paragraphs (see <a "
"class=\"pxref\" href=\"Paragraphs.html\">Paragraphs</a>), <kbd "
"class=\"kbd\">C-M-h</kbd> (<code class=\"code\">mark-defun</code>)  marks "
"top-level definitions (see <a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Moving-by-"
"Defuns.html\">Moving by Defuns</a>), and <kbd class=\"kbd\">C-x C-p</kbd> "
"(<code class=\"code\">mark-page</code>) marks pages (see <a class=\"pxref\" "
"href=\"Pages.html\">Pages</a>).  Repeated invocations again play the same "
"role, extending the region to consecutive objects; similarly, numeric "
"arguments specify how many objects to move the mark by."
msgstr ""
