# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#.  /@w 
#.  /@w 
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Matching.html
msgid ""
"Electric Pair mode is a minor mode that provides a way to easily insert "
"pairs of matching delimiters: parentheses, braces, brackets, quotes, etc. "
"(what counts as matching delimiters depends on the major mode).  To toggle "
"Electric Pair mode globally, type <kbd class=\"kbd\">M-x&nbsp;electric-pair-"
"mode</kbd>.  To toggle it only in the current buffer, type <kbd "
"class=\"kbd\">M-x&nbsp;electric-pair-local-mode</kbd>."
msgstr ""
"Electric Pairモードは、丸括弧、波括弧、角括弧、引用符などの対応する区切り文字"
"のペアを簡単に挿入できるマイナーモードです（何が対応する区切り文字とみなされ"
"るかは、メジャーモードによって異なります）。Electric Pairモードをグローバルに"
"切り替えるには、<kbd class=\"kbd\">M-x&nbsp;electric-pair-mode</kbd>と入力し"
"てください。現在のバッファのみで切り替えるには、<kbd class=\"kbd\">M-"
"x&nbsp;electric-pair-local-mode</kbd>と入力してください。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Matching.html
msgid ""
"When this mode is enabled, typing an opening delimiter inserts both that "
"character and, immediately following it, the matching closing delimiter, "
"leaving point between the two.  This makes it unnecessary to type a matching "
"closing delimiter in most cases.  If you type one nonetheless, Emacs simply "
"inserts that character, unless point is immediately before a closing "
"delimiter of the same type; in that case, point moves to immediately after "
"the closing delimiter and no additional closing delimiter is inserted.  "
"Thus, typing the sequence &lt;opening delimiter&gt;, &lt;matching closing "
"delimiter&gt; is a perhaps more convenient alternative to the sequence "
"&lt;opening delimiter&gt;, <kbd class=\"kbd\">C-f</kbd>."
msgstr ""
"このモードが有効な場合、開き区切り文字を入力すると、その文字と、それに続けて"
"対応する閉じ区切り文字の両方が挿入され、ポイントはその2文字の間に配置されま"
"す。これにより、ほとんどの場合、対応する閉じ区切り文字を入力する必要がなくな"
"ります。それでも閉じ区切り文字を入力した場合、ポイントが同種の閉じ区切り文字"
"の直前にない限り、Emacsは単にその文字を挿入します。その場合、ポイントは閉じ区"
"切り文字の直後に移動し、追加の閉じ区切り文字は挿入されません。したがって、"
"&lt;開き区切り文字&gt;, &lt;対応する閉じ区切り文字&gt; というシーケンスを入力"
"することは、&lt;開き区切り文字&gt;, <kbd class=\"kbd\">C-f</kbd> というシーケ"
"ンスに代わる、おそらくより便利な方法となります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Matching.html
msgid ""
"With an active region (see <a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Mark.html\">The Mark "
"and the Region</a>), Electric Pair mode operates differently: inserting "
"either an opening or a closing delimiter encloses the characters in the "
"region within the resulting pair of matching delimiters, leaving point after "
"the delimiter you typed (this facilitates continuing to type either before "
"the text following the opening delimiter or after the closing delimiter)."
msgstr ""
"アクティブリージョン（<a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Mark.html\">マークとリージョ"
"ン</a>を参照）がある場合、エレクトリックペアモードの動作は異なります。開きデ"
"リミタまたは閉じデリミタのいずれかを挿入すると、リージョン内の文字が結果とし"
"て得られた一対の対応デリミタで囲まれ、入力したデリミタの直後にポイントが残り"
"ます（これにより、開きデリミタに続くテキストの前、あるいは閉じデリミタの後の"
"いずれかで入力を続けることが容易になります）。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Matching.html
msgid ""
"If you provide a prefix argument when inserting an opening "
"delimiter&mdash;and if the region is active, also when inserting a closing "
"delimiter&mdash;this results in the insertion of as many nested pairs of "
"matching delimiters as the numeric value of that prefix argument."
msgstr ""
"開き区切り文字を挿入する際にプレフィックス引数を指定し&mdash;かつリージョンが"
"アクティブな場合は、閉じ区切り文字を挿入する際にも&mdash;これにより、そのプレ"
"フィックス引数の数値分だけ、対応する区切り文字の入れ子ペアが挿入されます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Matching.html
msgid ""
"There are several user options for modifying the behavior of Electric Pair "
"mode:"
msgstr ""
"Electric Pairモードの動作を変更するためのユーザーオプションがいくつか用意され"
"ています："

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li>
#: build/html/emacs/Matching.html
msgid ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-"
"electric_002dpair_002dpreserve_002dbalance\"></a> <code "
"class=\"code\">electric-pair-preserve-balance</code>, when non-<code "
"class=\"code\">nil</code> (the default), makes typing a delimiter preserve "
"the balance between opening and closing delimiters.  Thus, if you type an "
"opening delimiter and there is an unpaired matching closing delimiter later "
"in the buffer, then only the opening delimiter gets inserted (and not a "
"matching closing delimiter immediately following it); likewise, if there is "
"an unpaired opening delimiter, then typing a matching closing delimiter "
"later in the buffer inserts this character even when the following character "
"is another matching closing delimiter."
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Matching.html
msgid ""
"When set to <code class=\"code\">nil</code>, typing an opening delimiter "
"inserts only this character, but only when point is either immediately "
"before or immediately after a matching opening delimiter, or immediately "
"before a letter or digit; in all other positions inserting an opening "
"delimiter automatically inserts a matching closing delimiter immediately "
"following it, even if there is an unpaired matching closing delimiter later "
"in the buffer.  And typing a closing delimiter immediately before another "
"closing delimiter of the same type does not insert that character but moves "
"point as described above, even when there is an unpaired matching opening "
"delimiter earlier in the buffer."
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">nil</code> に設定されている場合、開きデリミタを入力する"
"と、この文字のみが挿入されます。ただし、ポイントが対応する開きデリミタの直前"
"または直後、あるいは英数字の直前にある場合に限ります。それ以外の位置で開きデ"
"リミタを入力すると、バッファの後方にペアになっていない対応する閉じデリミタが"
"存在していても、自動的にその直後に一致する閉じデリミタが挿入されます。また、"
"同じ種類の閉じデリミタの直前に閉じデリミタを入力しても、その文字は挿入され"
"ず、バッファの前方にペアになっていない対応する開きデリミタが存在していても、"
"前述の通りポイントが移動します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Matching.html
msgid "If there is an active region, this variable has no effect."
msgstr "活動領域がある場合、この変数は効果を持ちません。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li>
#: build/html/emacs/Matching.html
msgid ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-"
"electric_002dpair_002ddelete_002dadjacent_002dpairs\"></a> <code "
"class=\"code\">electric-pair-delete-adjacent-pairs</code>, when non-<code "
"class=\"code\">nil</code> (the default), makes deleting an opening delimiter "
"by typing the <kbd class=\"key\">DEL</kbd> key (which is normally the <kbd "
"class=\"key\">BACKSPACE</kbd> key; see <a class=\"pxref\" href=\"DEL-Does-"
"Not-Delete.html\">If <kbd class=\"key\">DEL</kbd> Fails to Delete</a>) "
"automatically also delete an immediately following matching closing "
"delimiter (but not if there are any characters&mdash;including just "
"whitespace&mdash;between the paired delimiters).  When set to <code "
"class=\"code\">nil</code>, typing <kbd class=\"key\">BACKSPACE</kbd> deletes "
"only the opening delimiter.  (Typing <kbd class=\"key\">BACKSPACE</kbd> to "
"delete a closing delimiter always deletes only this character.)"
msgstr ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-"
"electric_002dpair_002ddelete_002dadjacent_002dpairs\"></a> <code "
"class=\"code\">electric-pair-delete-adjacent-pairs</code> で、非 <code "
"class=\"code\">nil</code>（デフォルト）の場合、<kbd class=\"key\">DEL</kbd> "
"キー（通常は <kbd class=\"key\">BACKSPACE</kbd> キーです。<a class=\"pxref\" "
"href=\"DEL-Does-Not-Delete.html\"><kbd class=\"key\">DEL</kbd> で削除できない"
"場合</a> を参照）を入力して開始デリミタを削除すると、直後に続く対応する終了デ"
"リミタも自動的に削除されます（ただし、ペアとなるデリミタの間に、空白文字を含"
"む何らかの文字がある場合は除きます）。<code class=\"code\">nil</code> に設定"
"されている場合、<kbd class=\"key\">BACKSPACE</kbd> を入力すると開始デリミタの"
"みが削除されます。（<kbd class=\"key\">BACKSPACE</kbd> を入力して終了デリミタ"
"を削除すると、常にその文字のみが削除されます。）"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li>
#: build/html/emacs/Matching.html
msgid ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-"
"electric_002dpair_002dopen_002dnewline_002dbetween_002dpairs\"></a> When "
"<code class=\"code\">electric-pair-open-newline-between-pairs</code> is non-"
"<code class=\"code\">nil</code> (the default) and point is between an "
"opening delimiter and an immediately following matching closing delimiter, "
"then typing a newline automatically inserts an extra newline after point "
"(possibly indenting the empty line point is on, depending on the major "
"mode).  When set to <code class=\"code\">nil</code>, typing a newline "
"inserts only one newline before point, as usual."
msgstr ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-"
"electric_002dpair_002dopen_002dnewline_002dbetween_002dpairs\"></a> <code "
"class=\"code\">electric-pair-open-newline-between-pairs</code> が <code "
"class=\"code\">nil</code> 以外（デフォルト）であり、point が開きデリミタと、"
"その直後に続く対応する閉じデリミタとの間にある場合、改行を入力すると point の"
"後に自動的に余分な改行が挿入されます（メジャーモードによっては、point がある"
"空行がインデントされることがあります）。<code class=\"code\">nil</code> に設"
"定されている場合は、通常通り、改行を入力しても point の前に1行だけ改行が挿入"
"されます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li>
#: build/html/emacs/Matching.html
msgid ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-"
"electric_002dpair_002dskip_002dwhitespace\"></a> When <code "
"class=\"code\">electric-pair-skip-whitespace</code> has its default non-"
"<code class=\"code\">nil</code> value and point is separated from a closing "
"delimiter only by whitespace, then typing a closing delimiter of the same "
