# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><h3>
#: build/html/emacs/Misc-for-Programs.html
msgid ""
"<span>28.11 Other Features Useful for Editing Programs<a class=\"copiable-"
"link\" href=\"#Other-Features-Useful-for-Editing-Programs\"> &para;</a></"
"span>"
msgstr ""
"<span>28.11 プログラムの編集に役立つその他の機能<a class=\"copiable-link\" "
"href=\"#Other-Features-Useful-for-Editing-Programs\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Misc-for-Programs.html
msgid ""
"Some Emacs commands that aren&rsquo;t designed specifically for editing "
"programs are useful for that nonetheless."
msgstr ""
"プログラムの編集に特化して設計されたものではないEmacsコマンドの中にも、それで"
"も編集に役立つものがあります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Misc-for-Programs.html
msgid ""
"The Emacs commands that operate on words, sentences and paragraphs are "
"useful for editing code.  Most symbol names contain words (see <a "
"class=\"pxref\" href=\"Words.html\">Words</a>), while sentences can be found "
"in strings and comments (see <a class=\"pxref\" "
"href=\"Sentences.html\">Sentences</a>).  As for paragraphs, they are defined "
"in most programming language modes to begin and end at blank lines (see <a "
"class=\"pxref\" href=\"Paragraphs.html\">Paragraphs</a>).  Therefore, "
"judicious use of blank lines to make the program clearer will also provide "
"useful chunks of text for the paragraph commands to work on.  Auto Fill "
"mode, if enabled in a programming language major mode, indents the new lines "
"which it creates."
msgstr ""
"単語、文、段落を操作するEmacsコマンドは、コードの編集に便利です。ほとんどのシ"
"ンボル名には単語が含まれており（<a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Words.html\">単語</"
"a>を参照）、文は文字列やコメントの中に見られます（<a class=\"pxref\" "
"href=\"Sentences.html\">文</a>を参照）。段落については、ほとんどのプログラミ"
"ング言語モードにおいて、空行で始まり空行で終わるように定義されています（<a "
"class=\"pxref\" href=\"Paragraphs.html\">段落</a>を参照）。したがって、プログ"
"ラムをより分かりやすくするために空行を適切に活用すれば、段落コマンドが処理す"
"るための有用なテキスト塊を提供することにもなります。プログラミング言語メ"
"ジャーモードでAuto Fillモードが有効になっている場合、新たに作成される行はイン"
"デントされます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/emacs/Misc-for-Programs.html
msgid "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-superword_002dmode\"></a>"
msgstr "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-superword_002dmode\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Misc-for-Programs.html
msgid ""
"Superword mode is a buffer-local minor mode that causes editing and motion "
"commands to treat symbols (e.g., &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">this_is_a_symbol</samp>&rsquo;) as words.  When Superword "
"mode is enabled, the minor mode indicator &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">²</"
"samp>&rsquo; appears in the mode line.  See also the similar <code "
"class=\"code\">subword-mode</code> (see <a class=\"pxref\" href=\"MixedCase-"
"Words.html\">MixedCase Words</a>)."
msgstr ""
"Superwordモードは、編集コマンドや移動コマンドが記号（例：&lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">this_is_a_symbol</samp>&rsquo;）を単語として扱うようにするバッ"
"ファローカルなマイナーモードです。Superwordモードが有効になると、モードライン"
"にマイナーモードインジケータ &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">²</samp>&rsquo; が表"
"示されます。同様の <code class=\"code\">subword-mode</code> についても参照し"
"てください（<a class=\"pxref\" href=\"MixedCase-Words.html\">MixedCase "
"Words</a> を参照）。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/emacs/Misc-for-Programs.html
msgid ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-electric_002dlayout_002dmode\"></a>"
msgstr ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-electric_002dlayout_002dmode\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Misc-for-Programs.html
msgid ""
"Electric Layout mode (<kbd class=\"kbd\">M-x electric-layout-mode</kbd>) is "
"a global minor mode that automatically inserts newlines when you type "
"certain characters; for example, &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">{</"
"samp>&rsquo;, &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">}</samp>&rsquo; and &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">;</samp>&rsquo; in Javascript mode."
msgstr ""
"Electric Layoutモード (<kbd class=\"kbd\">M-x electric-layout-mode</kbd>) "
"は、特定の文字を入力した際に自動的に改行を挿入するグローバルマイナーモードで"
"す。例えば、JavaScriptモードにおける &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">{</"
"samp>&rsquo;、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">}</samp>&rsquo;、&lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">;</samp>&rsquo; などが該当します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Misc-for-Programs.html
msgid ""
"Apart from Hideshow mode (see <a class=\"pxref\" "
"href=\"Hideshow.html\">Hideshow minor mode</a>), another way to selectively "
"display parts of a program is to use the selective display feature (see <a "
"class=\"pxref\" href=\"Selective-Display.html\">Selective Display</a>).  "
"Programming modes often also support Outline minor mode (see <a "
"class=\"pxref\" href=\"Outline-Mode.html\">Outline Mode</a>), which can be "
"used with the Foldout package (see <a class=\"pxref\" "
"href=\"Foldout.html\">Folding Editing</a>)."
msgstr ""
"Hideshowモード（<a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Hideshow.html\">Hideshowマイナー"
"モード</a>を参照）以外に、プログラムの一部を選択的に表示するもう一つの方法と"
"して、選択的表示機能（<a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Selective-Display.html\">選択"
"的表示</a>を参照）を利用する方法があります。プログラミングモードでは、Outline"
"マイナーモード（<a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Outline-Mode.html\">Outlineモード</"
"a>を参照）もサポートされていることが多く、これはFoldoutパッケージ（<a "
"class=\"pxref\" href=\"Foldout.html\">折りたたみ編集</a>を参照）と組み合わせ"
"て使用できます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/emacs/Misc-for-Programs.html
msgid ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-prettify_002dsymbols_002dmode\"></a>"
msgstr ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-prettify_002dsymbols_002dmode\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Misc-for-Programs.html
msgid ""
"Prettify Symbols mode is a buffer-local minor mode that replaces certain "
"strings with more attractive versions for display purposes.  For example, in "
"Emacs Lisp mode, it replaces the string &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">lambda</"
"samp>&rsquo; with the Greek lambda character &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">λ</"
"samp>&rsquo;.  In a TeX buffer, it will replace &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">\\alpha</samp>&rsquo; &hellip; &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">\\omega</samp>&rsquo; and other math macros with their "
"Unicode characters.  You may wish to use this in non-programming modes as "
"well.  You can customize the mode by adding more entries to <code "
"class=\"code\">prettify-symbols-alist</code>.  More elaborate customization "
"is available via customizing <code class=\"code\">prettify-symbols-compose-"
"predicate</code> if its default value <code class=\"code\">prettify-symbols-"
"default-compose-p</code> is not appropriate.  There is also a global "
"version, <code class=\"code\">global-prettify-symbols-mode</code>, which "
"enables the mode in all buffers that support it."
msgstr ""
"Prettify Symbolsモードは、表示上の目的で特定の文字列をより見栄えの良い形式に"
"置き換える、バッファローカルなマイナーモードです。例えば、Emacs Lispモードで"
"は、文字列 &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">lambda</samp>&rsquo; をギリシャ文字の"
"ラムダ &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">λ</samp>&rsquo; に置き換えます。TeXバッ"
"ファでは、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\alpha</samp>&rsquo; &hellip; &lsquo;"
"<samp class=\"samp\">\\omega</samp>&rsquo; やその他の数学マクロを、それぞれの"
"Unicode文字に置き換えます。プログラミング以外のモードでも利用したい場合がある"
"でしょう。<code class=\"code\">prettify-symbols-alist</code>に項目を追加する"
"ことで、このモードをカスタマイズできます。デフォルト値の<code "
"class=\"code\">prettify-symbols-default-compose-p</code>が適切でない場合は、"
"<code class=\"code\">prettify-symbols-compose-predicate</code>をカスタマイズ"
"することで、より詳細な設定が可能です。また、グローバル版の<code "
"class=\"code\">global-prettify-symbols-mode</code>もあり、これを有効にする"
"と、このモードをサポートするすべてのバッファで動作します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Misc-for-Programs.html
msgid ""
"The symbol at point can be shown in its original form.  This is controlled "
"by the variable <code class=\"code\">prettify-symbols-unprettify-at-point</"
"code>: if non-<code class=\"code\">nil</code>, the original form of symbol "
"at point will be restored for as long as point is at it."
msgstr ""
"ポイントにあるシンボルを元の形式で表示できます。これは変数 <code "
"class=\"code\">prettify-symbols-unprettify-at-point</code> によって制御されま"
"す。<code class=\"code\">nil</code> でない場合、ポイントがそのシンボル上にあ"
"る限り、元の形式が復元されます。"

