#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Operating-on-Files.html
msgid ""
"If the directory you are visiting is under version control (see <a "
"class=\"pxref\" href=\"Version-Control.html\">Version Control</a>), then the "
"normal VC commands will operate on the selected files.  For example, <kbd "
"class=\"kbd\">C-x v v</kbd> invokes <code class=\"code\">dired-vc-next-"
"action</code>, which does the same as <code class=\"code\">vc-next-action</"
"code> in a buffer visiting a file under version control (see <a "
"class=\"pxref\" href=\"Basic-VC-Editing.html\">Basic Editing under Version "
"Control</a>).  Similarly, <kbd class=\"kbd\">C-x v =</kbd> shows the diffs "
"between the marked files and their committed versions, and <code "
"class=\"code\">C-x v l</code> shows the VC change history for the marked "
"files."
msgstr ""

