"a> <a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-"
"backward_002ddelete_002dchar_002duntabify\"></a>"
msgstr ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-DEL-_0028programming-modes_0029\"></"
"a> <a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-"
"backward_002ddelete_002dchar_002duntabify\"></a>"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Program-Modes.html
msgid ""
"In most programming languages, indentation should vary from line to line to "
"illustrate the structure of the program.  Therefore, in most programming "
"language modes, typing <kbd class=\"kbd\"><kbd class=\"key\">TAB</kbd></kbd> "
"updates the indentation of the current line (see <a class=\"pxref\" "
"href=\"Program-Indent.html\">Indentation for Programs</a>).  Furthermore, "
"<kbd class=\"kbd\"><kbd class=\"key\">DEL</kbd></kbd> is usually bound to "
"<code class=\"code\">backward-delete-char-untabify</code>, which deletes "
"backward treating each tab as if it were the equivalent number of spaces, so "
"that you can delete one column of indentation without worrying whether the "
"whitespace consists of spaces or tabs."
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/emacs/Program-Modes.html
msgid ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-mode-hook_002c-and-major-modes\"></a> "
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-c_002dmode_002dhook\"></a> <a "
"class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-lisp_002dmode_002dhook\"></a> <a "
"class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-emacs_002dlisp_002dmode_002dhook\"></a> "
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-"
"lisp_002dinteraction_002dmode_002dhook\"></a> <a class=\"index-entry-id\" "
"id=\"index-scheme_002dmode_002dhook\"></a>"
msgstr ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-mode-hook_002c-and-major-modes\"></a> "
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-c_002dmode_002dhook\"></a> <a "
"class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-lisp_002dmode_002dhook\"></a> <a "
"class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-emacs_002dlisp_002dmode_002dhook\"></a> "
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-"
"lisp_002dinteraction_002dmode_002dhook\"></a> <a class=\"index-entry-id\" "
"id=\"index-scheme_002dmode_002dhook\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Program-Modes.html
msgid ""
"Entering a programming language mode runs the custom Lisp functions "
"specified in the hook variable <code class=\"code\">prog-mode-hook</code>, "
"followed by those specified in the mode&rsquo;s own mode hook (see <a "
"class=\"pxref\" href=\"Major-Modes.html\">Major Modes</a>).  For instance, "
"entering C mode runs the hooks <code class=\"code\">prog-mode-hook</code> "
"and <code class=\"code\">c-mode-hook</code>.  See <a class=\"xref\" "
"href=\"Hooks.html\">Hooks</a>, for information about hooks."
msgstr ""
"プログラミング言語モードに入ると、フック変数 <code class=\"code\">prog-mode-"
"hook</code> で指定されたカスタムLisp関数が実行され、続いてそのモード自身の"
"モードフックで指定された関数が実行されます（<a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Major-"
"Modes.html\">メジャーモード</a>を参照）。例えば、Cモードに入ると、フック "
"<code class=\"code\">prog-mode-hook</code> と <code class=\"code\">c-mode-"
"hook</code> が実行されます。フックに関する情報については、<a class=\"xref\" "
"href=\"Hooks.html\">フック</a>を参照してください。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Program-Modes.html
msgid ""
"Separate manuals are available for the modes for Ada (see <a data-"
"manual=\"ada-mode\" href=\"https://elpa.gnu.org/packages/doc/ada-"
"mode.html#Top\">Ada Mode</a> in <cite class=\"cite\">Ada Mode</cite>), C/C++/"
"Objective C/Java/Corba IDL/Pike/AWK (see <a data-manual=\"ccmode\" "
"href=\"https://www.gnu.org/software/emacs/manual/html_node/ccmode/"
"index.html#Top\">CC Mode</a> in <cite class=\"cite\">CC Mode</cite>), "
"Octave, and VHDL."
msgstr ""
"Ada（<cite class=\"cite\">Ada Mode</cite>の<a data-manual=\"ada-mode\" "
"href=\"https://elpa.gnu.org/packages/doc/ada-mode.html#Top\">Ada Mode</a>を参"
"照）、C/C++/Objective C/Java/Corba IDL/Pike/AWK（<cite class=\"cite\">CC "
"Mode</cite>の<a data-manual=\"ccmode\" href=\"https://www.gnu.org/software/"
"emacs/manual/html_node/ccmode/index.html#Top\">CC Mode</a>を参照）、Octave、"
"およびVHDLの各モード向けに、個別のマニュアルが用意されています。"

