# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#.  /@w 
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Project-File-Commands.html
msgid ""
"<kbd class=\"kbd\">C-x p r</kbd> (<code class=\"code\">project-query-replace-"
"regexp</code>) is similar to <code class=\"code\">project-search</code>, but "
"it prompts you for whether to replace each match it finds, like <code "
"class=\"code\">query-replace</code> does (see <a class=\"pxref\" "
"href=\"Query-Replace.html\">Query Replace</a>), and continues to the next "
"match after you respond.  If your response causes Emacs to exit the query-"
"replace loop, you can later continue with <kbd class=\"kbd\">M-"
"x&nbsp;fileloop-continue&nbsp;<kbd class=\"key\">RET</kbd></kbd>."
msgstr ""
"<kbd class=\"kbd\">C-x p r</kbd> (<code class=\"code\">project-query-replace-"
"regexp</code>) は <code class=\"code\">project-search</code> と同様ですが、"
"<code class=\"code\">query-replace</code> のように見つかった各マッチを置換す"
"るかどうかをユーザーに問いかけ（<a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Query-"
"Replace.html\">Query Replace</a> を参照）、回答後に次のマッチへと進みます。回"
"答によって Emacs が query-replace ループを終了した場合は、後で <kbd "
"class=\"kbd\">M-x&nbsp;fileloop-continue&nbsp;<kbd class=\"key\">RET</kbd></"
"kbd> から再開できます。"

