# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><h3>
#: build/html/emacs/Regexp-Backslash.html
msgid ""
"<span>17.7 Backslash in Regular Expressions<a class=\"copiable-link\" "
"href=\"#Backslash-in-Regular-Expressions\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span>17.7 正規表現におけるバックスラッシュ<a class=\"copiable-link\" "
"href=\"#Backslash-in-Regular-Expressions\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Regexp-Backslash.html
msgid ""
"For the most part, &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\</samp>&rsquo; followed by "
"any character matches only that character.  However, there are several "
"exceptions: two-character sequences starting with &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">\\</samp>&rsquo; that have special meanings.  The second "
"character in the sequence is always an ordinary character when used on its "
"own.  Here is a table of &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\</samp>&rsquo; "
"constructs."
msgstr ""
"ほとんどの場合、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\</samp>&rsquo; に続く任意の文字"
"は、その文字にのみ一致します。ただし、いくつかの例外があります。&lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">\\</samp>&rsquo; で始まる2文字のシーケンスは、特別な意味を持ち"
"ます。このシーケンスの2文字目は、単独で使用される場合は常に通常の文字となりま"
"す。以下に &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\</samp>&rsquo; 構文の表を示します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/emacs/Regexp-Backslash.html
msgid "<kbd class=\"kbd\">\\|</kbd>"
msgstr "<kbd class=\"kbd\">\\|</kbd>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Regexp-Backslash.html
msgid ""
"specifies an alternative.  Two regular expressions <var class=\"var\">a</"
"var> and <var class=\"var\">b</var> with &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\|</"
"samp>&rsquo; in between form an expression that matches some text if either "
"<var class=\"var\">a</var> matches it or <var class=\"var\">b</var> matches "
"it.  It works by trying to match <var class=\"var\">a</var>, and if that "
"fails, by trying to match <var class=\"var\">b</var>."
msgstr ""
"代替パターンを指定します。<var class=\"var\">a</var> と <var "
"class=\"var\">b</var> という2つの正規表現の間に &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">\\|</samp>&rsquo; を挟んだ表現は、<var class=\"var\">a</var> "
"または <var class=\"var\">b</var> のいずれかがマッチした場合に、そのテキスト"
"にマッチします。これは、まず <var class=\"var\">a</var> のマッチを試み、それ"
"が失敗した場合に <var class=\"var\">b</var> のマッチを試みることで動作しま"
"す。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Regexp-Backslash.html
msgid ""
"Thus, &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">foo\\|bar</samp>&rsquo; matches either "
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">foo</samp>&rsquo; or &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">bar</samp>&rsquo; but no other string."
msgstr ""
"したがって、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">foo\\|bar</samp>&rsquo;は&lsquo;"
"<samp class=\"samp\">foo</samp>&rsquo;または&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">bar</"
"samp>&rsquo;のいずれかにマッチしますが、それ以外の文字列にはマッチしません。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Regexp-Backslash.html
msgid ""
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\|</samp>&rsquo; applies to the largest "
"possible surrounding expressions.  Only a surrounding &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">\\( &hellip; \\)</samp>&rsquo; grouping can limit the "
"grouping power of &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\|</samp>&rsquo;."
msgstr ""
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\|</samp>&rsquo;は、取り得る最大の周辺式に適用さ"
"れます。&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\|</samp>&rsquo;のグループ化能力を制限で"
"きるのは、周囲の&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\( &hellip; \\)</samp>&rsquo;グ"
"ループのみです。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Regexp-Backslash.html
msgid ""
"Full backtracking capability exists to handle multiple uses of &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">\\|</samp>&rsquo;."
msgstr ""
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\|</samp>&rsquo;の複数回の使用に対応できるよう、"
"完全なバックトラッキング機能が備わっています。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/emacs/Regexp-Backslash.html
msgid ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-grouping_002c-in-regular-"
"expressions\"></a> <a id=\"index-sub_002dexpressions_002c-in-regular-"
"expressions\"></a><span><kbd class=\"kbd\">\\( &hellip; \\)</kbd><a "
"class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-sub_002dexpressions_002c-in-regular-"
"expressions\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-grouping_002c-in-regular-"
"expressions\"></a> <a id=\"index-sub_002dexpressions_002c-in-regular-"
"expressions\"></a><span><kbd class=\"kbd\">\\( &hellip; \\)</kbd><a "
"class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-sub_002dexpressions_002c-in-regular-"
"expressions\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Regexp-Backslash.html
msgid "is a grouping construct that serves three purposes:"
msgstr "は、3つの目的を果たすグループ化構文です："

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><ol><li>
#: build/html/emacs/Regexp-Backslash.html
msgid ""
"To enclose a set of &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\|</samp>&rsquo; "
"alternatives for other operations.  Thus, &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\"
"(foo\\|bar\\)x</samp>&rsquo; matches either &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">foox</samp>&rsquo; or &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">barx</"
"samp>&rsquo;."
msgstr ""
"他の操作のための &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\|</samp>&rsquo; の選択肢群を囲"
"む。これにより、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\(foo\\|bar\\)x</samp>&rsquo; "
"は &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">foox</samp>&rsquo; または &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">barx</samp>&rsquo; のいずれかにマッチする。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><ol><li>
#: build/html/emacs/Regexp-Backslash.html
msgid ""
"To enclose a complicated expression for the postfix operators &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">*</samp>&rsquo;, &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">+</samp>&rsquo; "
"and &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">?</samp>&rsquo; to operate on.  Thus, &lsquo;"
"<samp class=\"samp\">ba\\(na\\)*</samp>&rsquo; matches &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">bananana</samp>&rsquo;, etc., with any (zero or more) number "
"of &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">na</samp>&rsquo; strings."
msgstr ""
"後置演算子 &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">*</samp>&rsquo;、&lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">+</samp>&rsquo;、および &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">?</"
"samp>&rsquo; が作用する複雑な式を囲むため。これにより、&lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">ba\\(na\\)*</samp>&rsquo; は、任意の数（0個以上）の &lsquo;"
"<samp class=\"samp\">na</samp>&rsquo; 文字列を伴う &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">bananana</samp>&rsquo; などにマッチします。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><ol><li>
#: build/html/emacs/Regexp-Backslash.html
msgid "To record a matched substring for future reference."
msgstr "後で参照するために、一致した部分文字列を記録する。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#.  /@w 
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Regexp-Backslash.html
msgid ""
"This last application is not a consequence of the idea of a parenthetical "
"grouping; it is a separate feature that is assigned as a second meaning to "
"the same &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\(&nbsp;&hellip;&nbsp;\\)</"
"samp>&rsquo; construct.  In practice there is usually no conflict between "
"the two meanings; when there is a conflict, you can use a shy group, "
"described below."
msgstr ""
"この最後の用法は、括弧書きのグループ化という考え方から生じたものではなく、同"
"一の &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\(&nbsp;&hellip;&nbsp;\\)</samp>&rsquo; 構"
"文に第2の意味として割り当てられた独立した機能です。実際には、通常これら2つの"
"意味の間で衝突が生じることはありません。衝突が生じる場合には、後述するシャイ"
"グループを使用できます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/emacs/Regexp-Backslash.html
msgid ""
"<a id=\"index-shy-group_002c-in-regexp\"></a><span><kbd class=\"kbd\">\\(?: "
"&hellip; \\)</kbd><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-shy-group_002c-in-"
"regexp\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<a id=\"index-shy-group_002c-in-regexp\"></a><span><kbd class=\"kbd\">\\(?: "
"&hellip; \\)</kbd><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-shy-group_002c-in-"
"regexp\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Regexp-Backslash.html
msgid ""
"specifies a <em class=\"dfn\">shy group</em> that does not record the "
"matched substring; you can&rsquo;t refer back to it with &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">\\<var class=\"var\">d</var></samp>&rsquo; (see below).  This "
"is useful in mechanically combining regular expressions, so that you can add "
"groups for syntactic purposes without interfering with the numbering of the "
"groups that are meant to be referred to."
msgstr ""
"マッチした部分文字列を記録しない<em class=\"dfn\">シャイグループ</em>を指定し"
"ます。「<samp class=\"samp\">\\<var class=\"var\">d</var></samp>」を用いてこ"
"のグループを参照することはできません（後述）。これは、正規表現を機械的に結合"
"する際に有用で、参照対象となるグループの番号付けに影響を与えることなく、構文"
"上の目的でグループを追加できます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/emacs/Regexp-Backslash.html
msgid ""
"<a id=\"index-back-reference_002c-in-regexp\"></a><span><kbd "
"class=\"kbd\">\\<var class=\"var\">d</var></kbd><a class=\"copiable-link\" "
"href=\"#index-back-reference_002c-in-regexp\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<a id=\"index-back-reference_002c-in-regexp\"></a><span><kbd "
"class=\"kbd\">\\<var class=\"var\">d</var></kbd><a class=\"copiable-link\" "
"href=\"#index-back-reference_002c-in-regexp\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Regexp-Backslash.html
msgid ""
"matches the same text that matched the <var class=\"var\">d</var>th "
"occurrence of a &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\( &hellip; \\)</samp>&rsquo; "
"construct.  This is called a <em class=\"dfn\">back reference</em>."
msgstr ""
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\( &hellip; \\)</samp>&rsquo; 構文の <var "
"class=\"var\">d</var> 回目の出現にマッチしたのと同じテキストにマッチします。"
"これを <em class=\"dfn\">後方参照</em> と呼びます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Regexp-Backslash.html
msgid ""
"After the end of a &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\( &hellip; \\)</"
"samp>&rsquo; construct, the matcher remembers the beginning and end of the "
"text matched by that construct.  Then, later on in the regular expression, "
"you can use &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\</samp>&rsquo; followed by the "
"digit <var class=\"var\">d</var> to mean &ldquo;match the same text matched "
"the <var class=\"var\">d</var>th &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\( &hellip; "
"\\)</samp>&rsquo; construct&rdquo;."
msgstr ""
"「<samp class=\"samp\">\\( &hellip; \\)</samp>」という構文が終了した後、マッ"
"チャーはその構文でマッチしたテキストの開始位置と終了位置を記憶します。その"
"後、正規表現の続きで、「<samp class=\"samp\">\\</samp>」に数字の<var "
"class=\"var\">d</var>を続けることで、「<var class=\"var\">d</var>番目の<samp "
"class=\"samp\">\\( &hellip; \\)</samp>構文でマッチしたのと同じテキストにマッ"
"チする」という意味を表現できます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Regexp-Backslash.html
msgid ""
"The strings matching the first nine &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\( &hellip; "
"\\)</samp>&rsquo; constructs appearing in a regular expression are assigned "
"numbers 1 through 9 in the order that the open-parentheses appear in the "
"regular expression.  So you can use &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\1</"
"samp>&rsquo; through &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\9</samp>&rsquo; to refer "
"to the text matched by the corresponding &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\"
"( &hellip; \\)</samp>&rsquo; constructs."
msgstr ""
"正規表現に現れる最初の9つの &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\( &hellip; \\)</"
"samp>&rsquo; 構文に一致する文字列には、正規表現内で開き括弧が現れる順に1から9"
"までの番号が割り当てられます。したがって、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\1</"
"samp>&rsquo; から &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\9</samp>&rsquo; を用いて、対"
"応する &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\( &hellip; \\)</samp>&rsquo; 構文に一致"
"するテキストを参照できます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Regexp-Backslash.html
msgid ""
"For example, &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\(.*\\)\\1</samp>&rsquo; matches "
"any newline-free string that is composed of two identical halves.  The "
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\(.*\\)</samp>&rsquo; matches the first half, "
"which may be anything, but the &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\1</samp>&rsquo; "
"that follows must match the same exact text."
msgstr ""
"例えば、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\(.*\\)\\1</samp>&rsquo;は、同一の2つの"
"部分から構成される改行を含まない任意の文字列にマッチします。&lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">\\(.*\\)</samp>&rsquo;は前半部分にマッチし、その内容は任意です"
"が、それに続く&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\1</samp>&rsquo;は全く同じテキスト"
"にマッチしなければなりません。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Regexp-Backslash.html
msgid ""
"If a particular &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\( &hellip; \\)</samp>&rsquo; "
"construct matches more than once (which can easily happen if it is followed "
"by &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">*</samp>&rsquo;), only the last match is "
"recorded."
msgstr ""
"特定の &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\( &hellip; \\)</samp>&rsquo; 構文が複数"
"回マッチした場合（その後に &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">*</samp>&rsquo; が続く"
"場合などに容易に起こり得ます）、最後のマッチのみが記録されます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/emacs/Regexp-Backslash.html
msgid ""
"<kbd class=\"kbd\"><kbd class=\"kbd\">\\{<var class=\"var\">m</var>\\}</"
"kbd></kbd>"
msgstr ""
"<kbd class=\"kbd\"><kbd class=\"kbd\">\\{<var class=\"var\">m</var>\\}</"
"kbd></kbd>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Regexp-Backslash.html
msgid ""
"is a postfix operator specifying <var class=\"var\">m</var> "
"repetitions&mdash;that is, the preceding regular expression must match "
"exactly <var class=\"var\">m</var> times in a row.  For example, &lsquo;"
"<samp class=\"samp\">x\\{4\\}</samp>&rsquo; matches the string &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">xxxx</samp>&rsquo; and nothing else."
msgstr ""
"は、<var class=\"var\">m</var>回の繰り返しを指定する後置演算子です。つまり、"
"直前の正規表現が連続してちょうど<var class=\"var\">m</var>回マッチする必要が"
"あります。例えば、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">x\\{4\\}</samp>&rsquo;は文字列"
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">xxxx</samp>&rsquo;にのみマッチし、それ以外には"
"マッチしません。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/emacs/Regexp-Backslash.html
msgid ""
"<kbd class=\"kbd\"><kbd class=\"kbd\">\\{<var class=\"var\">m</var>,<var "
"class=\"var\">n</var>\\}</kbd></kbd>"
msgstr ""
"<kbd class=\"kbd\"><kbd class=\"kbd\">\\{<var class=\"var\">m</var>,<var "
"class=\"var\">n</var>\\}</kbd></kbd>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Regexp-Backslash.html
msgid ""
"is a postfix operator specifying between <var class=\"var\">m</var> and <var "
"class=\"var\">n</var> repetitions&mdash;that is, the preceding regular "
"expression must match at least <var class=\"var\">m</var> times, but no more "
"than <var class=\"var\">n</var> times.  If <var class=\"var\">n</var> is "
"omitted, then there is no upper limit, but the preceding regular expression "
"must match at least <var class=\"var\">m</var> times."
msgstr ""
"は、<var class=\"var\">m</var> から <var class=\"var\">n</var> 回の繰り返しを"
"指定する後置演算子です。つまり、直前の正規表現は少なくとも <var "
"class=\"var\">m</var> 回、最大で <var class=\"var\">n</var> 回マッチする必要"
"があります。<var class=\"var\">n</var> を省略した場合は上限はありませんが、直"
"前の正規表現は少なくとも <var class=\"var\">m</var> 回マッチする必要がありま"
"す。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p><br>
#: build/html/emacs/Regexp-Backslash.html
msgid ""
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\{0,1\\}</samp>&rsquo; is equivalent to &lsquo;"
"<samp class=\"samp\">?</samp>&rsquo;."
msgstr ""
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\{0,1\\}</samp>&rsquo;は&lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">?</samp>&rsquo;と等価です。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p><br><br>
#: build/html/emacs/Regexp-Backslash.html
msgid ""
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\{0,\\}</samp>&rsquo; is equivalent to &lsquo;"
"<samp class=\"samp\">*</samp>&rsquo;."
msgstr ""
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\{0,\\}</samp>&rsquo;は&lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">*</samp>&rsquo;と等価です。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p><br><br><br>
#: build/html/emacs/Regexp-Backslash.html
msgid ""
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\{1,\\}</samp>&rsquo; is equivalent to &lsquo;"
"<samp class=\"samp\">+</samp>&rsquo;."
msgstr ""
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\{1,\\}</samp>&rsquo;は&lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">+</samp>&rsquo;と等価です。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/emacs/Regexp-Backslash.html
msgid "<kbd class=\"kbd\">\\`</kbd>"
msgstr "<kbd class=\"kbd\">\\`</kbd>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Regexp-Backslash.html
msgid ""
"matches the empty string, but only at the beginning of the string or buffer "
"(or its accessible portion) being matched against."
msgstr ""
"空文字列に一致しますが、照合対象の文字列またはバッファ（あるいはそのアクセス"
"可能な部分）の先頭においてのみ一致します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/emacs/Regexp-Backslash.html
msgid "<kbd class=\"kbd\">\\'</kbd>"
msgstr "<kbd class=\"kbd\">\\'</kbd>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Regexp-Backslash.html
msgid ""
"matches the empty string, but only at the end of the string or buffer (or "
"its accessible portion) being matched against."
msgstr ""
"空文字列に一致しますが、照合対象の文字列またはバッファ（あるいはそのアクセス"
"可能な部分）の末尾においてのみ一致します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/emacs/Regexp-Backslash.html
msgid "<kbd class=\"kbd\">\\=</kbd>"
msgstr "<kbd class=\"kbd\">\\=</kbd>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Regexp-Backslash.html
msgid "matches the empty string, but only at point."
msgstr "空文字列に一致するが、一点のみ。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/emacs/Regexp-Backslash.html
msgid "<kbd class=\"kbd\">\\b</kbd>"
msgstr "<kbd class=\"kbd\">\\b</kbd>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Regexp-Backslash.html
msgid ""
"matches the empty string, but only at the beginning or end of a word.  Thus, "
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\bfoo\\b</samp>&rsquo; matches any occurrence "
"of &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">foo</samp>&rsquo; as a separate word.  &lsquo;"
"<samp class=\"samp\">\\bballs?\\b</samp>&rsquo; matches &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">ball</samp>&rsquo; or &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">balls</"
"samp>&rsquo; as a separate word."
msgstr ""
"空文字列にマッチしますが、単語の先頭または末尾にある場合に限られます。した"
"がって、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\bfoo\\b</samp>&rsquo;は、独立した単語と"
"しての&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">foo</samp>&rsquo;のあらゆる出現箇所にマッチ"
"します。&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\bballs?\\b</samp>&rsquo;は、独立した単"
"語としての&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">ball</samp>&rsquo;または&lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">balls</samp>&rsquo;にマッチします。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Regexp-Backslash.html
msgid ""
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\b</samp>&rsquo; matches at the beginning or "
"end of the buffer regardless of what text appears next to it."
msgstr ""
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\b</samp>&rsquo;は、直後にどのようなテキストが続"
"いていても、バッファの先頭または末尾にマッチします。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/emacs/Regexp-Backslash.html
msgid "<kbd class=\"kbd\">\\B</kbd>"
msgstr "<kbd class=\"kbd\">\\B</kbd>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Regexp-Backslash.html
msgid ""
"matches the empty string, but <em class=\"emph\">not</em> at the beginning "
"or end of a word."
msgstr ""
"空文字列に一致しますが、単語の先頭や末尾では<em class=\"emph\">一致しません</"
"em>。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/emacs/Regexp-Backslash.html
msgid "<kbd class=\"kbd\">\\&lt;</kbd>"
msgstr "<kbd class=\"kbd\">\\&lt;</kbd>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Regexp-Backslash.html
msgid ""
"matches the empty string, but only at the beginning of a word.  &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">\\&lt;</samp>&rsquo; matches at the beginning of the buffer "
"only if a word-constituent character follows."
msgstr ""
"空文字列にマッチしますが、単語の先頭である場合に限ります。&lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">\\&lt;</samp>&rsquo;は、単語構成文字が続く場合に限り、バッファ"
"の先頭にマッチします。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/emacs/Regexp-Backslash.html
msgid "<kbd class=\"kbd\">\\&gt;</kbd>"
msgstr "<kbd class=\"kbd\">\\&gt;</kbd>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Regexp-Backslash.html
msgid ""
"matches the empty string, but only at the end of a word.  &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">\\&gt;</samp>&rsquo; matches at the end of the buffer only if "
"the contents end with a word-constituent character."
msgstr ""
"空文字列にマッチしますが、単語の末尾に限られます。&lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">\\&gt;</samp>&rsquo;は、バッファの内容が単語構成文字で終わって"
"いる場合にのみ、バッファの末尾にマッチします。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/emacs/Regexp-Backslash.html
msgid "<kbd class=\"kbd\">\\w</kbd>"
msgstr "<kbd class=\"kbd\">\\w</kbd>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Regexp-Backslash.html
msgid ""
"matches any word-constituent character.  The syntax table determines which "
"characters these are.  See <a data-manual=\"elisp\" href=\"https://"
"www.gnu.org/software/emacs/manual/html_node/elisp/Syntax-Tables.html#Syntax-"
"Tables\">Syntax Tables</a> in <cite class=\"cite\">The Emacs Lisp Reference "
"Manual</cite>."
msgstr ""
"単語を構成する任意の文字に一致します。どの文字がこれに該当するかは、構文テー"
"ブルによって決定されます。<cite class=\"cite\">The Emacs Lisp Reference "
"Manual</cite>の<a data-manual=\"elisp\" href=\"https://www.gnu.org/software/"
"emacs/manual/html_node/elisp/Syntax-Tables.html#Syntax-Tables\">構文テーブル"
"</a>を参照してください。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/emacs/Regexp-Backslash.html
msgid "<kbd class=\"kbd\">\\W</kbd>"
msgstr "<kbd class=\"kbd\">\\W</kbd>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Regexp-Backslash.html
msgid "matches any character that is not a word-constituent."
msgstr "単語構成文字以外の任意の文字に一致します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/emacs/Regexp-Backslash.html
msgid "<kbd class=\"kbd\">\\_&lt;</kbd>"
msgstr "<kbd class=\"kbd\">\\_&lt;</kbd>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Regexp-Backslash.html
msgid ""
"matches the empty string, but only at the beginning of a symbol.  A symbol "
"is a sequence of one or more symbol-constituent characters.  A symbol-"
"constituent character is a character whose syntax is either &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">w</samp>&rsquo; or &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">_</"
"samp>&rsquo;.  &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\_&lt;</samp>&rsquo; matches at "
"the beginning of the buffer only if a symbol-constituent character follows.  "
"As with words, the syntax table determines which characters are symbol-"
"constituent."
msgstr ""
"空文字列にマッチしますが、シンボルの先頭である場合に限ります。シンボルとは、1"
"つ以上のシンボル構成文字の並びのことです。シンボル構成文字とは、その構文が "
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">w</samp>&rsquo; または &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">_</samp>&rsquo; である文字のことです。&lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">\\_&lt;</samp>&rsquo; は、その後にシンボル構成文字が続く場合に"
"のみ、バッファの先頭でマッチします。単語と同様に、どの文字がシンボル構成文字"
"であるかは構文テーブルによって決定されます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/emacs/Regexp-Backslash.html
msgid "<kbd class=\"kbd\">\\_&gt;</kbd>"
msgstr "<kbd class=\"kbd\">\\_&gt;</kbd>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Regexp-Backslash.html
msgid ""
"matches the empty string, but only at the end of a symbol.  &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">\\_&gt;</samp>&rsquo; matches at the end of the buffer only "
"if the contents end with a symbol-constituent character."
msgstr ""
"空文字列にマッチしますが、シンボルの末尾である場合に限られます。&lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">\\_&gt;</samp>&rsquo;がバッファの末尾にマッチするのは、内容が"
"シンボル構成文字で終わっている場合のみです。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/emacs/Regexp-Backslash.html
msgid "<kbd class=\"kbd\">\\s<var class=\"var\">c</var></kbd>"
msgstr "<kbd class=\"kbd\">\\s<var class=\"var\">c</var></kbd>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Regexp-Backslash.html
msgid ""
"matches any character whose syntax is <var class=\"var\">c</var>.  Here <var "
"class=\"var\">c</var> is a character that designates a particular syntax "
"class: thus, &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">w</samp>&rsquo; for word "
