# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Regexps.html
msgid ""
"This section (and this manual in general) describes regular expression "
"features that users typically use.  See <a data-manual=\"elisp\" "
"href=\"https://www.gnu.org/software/emacs/manual/html_node/elisp/Regular-"
"Expressions.html#Regular-Expressions\">Regular Expressions</a> in <cite "
"class=\"cite\">The Emacs Lisp Reference Manual</cite>, for additional "
"features used mainly in Lisp programs."
msgstr ""
"本節（および本マニュアル全般）では、ユーザーが通常利用する正規表現の機能につ"
"いて解説します。主にLispプログラムで使用されるその他の機能については、<cite "
"class=\"cite\">The Emacs Lisp Reference Manual</cite>の<a data-"
"manual=\"elisp\" href=\"https://www.gnu.org/software/emacs/manual/html_node/"
"elisp/Regular-Expressions.html#Regular-Expressions\">Regular Expressions</a>"
"を参照してください。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Regexps.html
msgid ""
"Regular expressions have a syntax in which a few characters are <em "
"class=\"dfn\">special constructs</em> and the rest are <em "
"class=\"dfn\">ordinary</em>.  An ordinary character matches that same "
"character and nothing else.  The special characters are &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">$^.*+?[\\</samp>&rsquo;.  The character &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">]</samp>&rsquo; is special if it ends a bracket expression "
"(see below).  The character &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">-</samp>&rsquo; is "
"special inside a bracket expression.  Any other character appearing in a "
"regular expression is ordinary, unless a &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\</"
"samp>&rsquo; precedes it.  (When you use regular expressions in a Lisp "
"program, each &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\</samp>&rsquo; must be doubled, "
"see the example near the end of this section.)"
msgstr ""
"正規表現には、少数の文字が<em class=\"dfn\">特殊構文</em>であり、それ以外は"
"<em class=\"dfn\">通常文字</em>であるという構文があります。通常文字は、それ自"
"身にのみ一致し、それ以外には一致しません。特殊文字は&lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">$^.*+?[\\</samp>&rsquo;です。&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">]</"
"samp>&rsquo;という文字は、括弧式（後述）の末尾にある場合に特殊となります。"
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">-</samp>&rsquo;という文字は、括弧式の中では特殊と"
"なります。正規表現に現れるその他の文字は、その前に&lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">\\</samp>&rsquo;がない限り、通常文字となります。（Lispプログラ"
"ムで正規表現を使用する場合、各&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\</samp>&rsquo;は2"
"回記述する必要があります。本節の終盤にある例を参照してください。）"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Regexps.html
msgid ""
"For example, &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">f</samp>&rsquo; is not a special "
"character, so it is ordinary, and therefore &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">f</"
"samp>&rsquo; is a regular expression that matches the string &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">f</samp>&rsquo; and no other string.  (It does <em "
"class=\"emph\">not</em> match the string &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">ff</"
"samp>&rsquo;.)  Likewise, &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">o</samp>&rsquo; is a "
"regular expression that matches only &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">o</"
"samp>&rsquo;.  (When case distinctions are being ignored, these regexps also "
"match &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">F</samp>&rsquo; and &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">O</samp>&rsquo;, but we consider this a generalization of "
"&ldquo;the same string&rdquo;, rather than an exception.)"
msgstr ""
"例えば、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">f</samp>&rsquo;は特殊文字ではないため通常"
"の文字であり、したがって&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">f</samp>&rsquo;は文字列"
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">f</samp>&rsquo;にのみマッチし、それ以外の文字列に"
"はマッチしない正規表現となります。（文字列&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">ff</"
"samp>&rsquo;には<em class=\"emph\">マッチしません</em>。）同様に、&lsquo;"
"<samp class=\"samp\">o</samp>&rsquo;は&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">o</"
"samp>&rsquo;にのみマッチする正規表現です。（大文字小文字を区別しない場合、こ"
"れらの正規表現は&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">F</samp>&rsquo;や&lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">O</samp>&rsquo;にもマッチしますが、これは例外ではなく、「同一"
"の文字列」の一般化であると考えています。）"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Regexps.html
msgid ""
"Any two regular expressions <var class=\"var\">a</var> and <var "
"class=\"var\">b</var> can be concatenated.  The result is a regular "
"expression which matches a string if <var class=\"var\">a</var> matches some "
"amount of the beginning of that string and <var class=\"var\">b</var> "
"matches the rest of the string.  As a trivial example, concatenating the "
"regular expressions &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">f</samp>&rsquo; and &lsquo;"
"<samp class=\"samp\">o</samp>&rsquo; gives the regular expression &lsquo;"
"<samp class=\"samp\">fo</samp>&rsquo;, which matches only the string &lsquo;"
"<samp class=\"samp\">fo</samp>&rsquo;.  To do something less trivial, you "
"need to use one of the special characters.  Here is a list of them."
msgstr ""
"任意の2つの正規表現 <var class=\"var\">a</var> と <var class=\"var\">b</var> "
"は連結できます。その結果得られる正規表現は、<var class=\"var\">a</var> がその"
"文字列の先頭の一定部分にマッチし、かつ <var class=\"var\">b</var> が文字列の"
"残りの部分にマッチする場合に、その文字列にマッチします。簡単な例として、正規"
"表現 &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">f</samp>&rsquo; と &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">o</samp>&rsquo; を連結すると正規表現 &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">fo</samp>&rsquo; が得られ、これは文字列 &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">fo</samp>&rsquo; にのみマッチします。より複雑な処理を行うに"
"は、特殊文字のいずれかを使用する必要があります。以下にその一覧を示します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/emacs/Regexps.html
msgid "<kbd class=\"kbd\">.</kbd> <span class=\"r\">(Period)</span>"
msgstr "<kbd class=\"kbd\">.</kbd> <span class=\"r\">（期間）</span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Regexps.html
msgid ""
"is a special character that matches any single character except a newline.  "
"For example, the regular expressions &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">a.b</"
"samp>&rsquo; matches any three-character string that begins with &lsquo;"
"<samp class=\"samp\">a</samp>&rsquo; and ends with &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">b</samp>&rsquo;."
msgstr ""
"は、改行を除く任意の1文字にマッチする特殊文字です。例えば、正規表現 &lsquo;"
"<samp class=\"samp\">a.b</samp>&rsquo; は、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">a</"
"samp>&rsquo; で始まり &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">b</samp>&rsquo; で終わる任"
"意の3文字の文字列にマッチします。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/emacs/Regexps.html
msgid "<kbd class=\"kbd\">*</kbd>"
msgstr "<kbd class=\"kbd\">*</kbd>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Regexps.html
msgid ""
"is not a construct by itself; it is a postfix operator that means to match "
"the preceding regular expression repetitively any number of times, as many "
"times as possible.  Thus, &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">o*</samp>&rsquo; "
"matches any number of &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">o</samp>&rsquo;s, "
"including no &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">o</samp>&rsquo;s."
msgstr ""
"それ自体は構成要素ではなく、直前の正規表現を任意の回数、可能な限り繰り返し"
"マッチさせることを意味する後置演算子です。したがって、&lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">o*</samp>&rsquo;は、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">o</"
"samp>&rsquo;が一つも含まれない場合も含め、任意の数の&lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">o</samp>&rsquo;にマッチします。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Regexps.html
msgid ""
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">*</samp>&rsquo; always applies to the <em "
"class=\"emph\">smallest</em> possible preceding expression.  Thus, &lsquo;"
"<samp class=\"samp\">fo*</samp>&rsquo; has a repeating &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">o</samp>&rsquo;, not a repeating &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">fo</samp>&rsquo;.  It matches &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">f</"
"samp>&rsquo;, &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">fo</samp>&rsquo;, &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">foo</samp>&rsquo;, and so on."
msgstr ""
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">*</samp>&rsquo;は常に、直前の<em class=\"emph\">"
"最小</em>の式に適用されます。したがって、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">fo*</"
"samp>&rsquo;に繰り返し現れるのは&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">o</samp>&rsquo;で"
"あり、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">fo</samp>&rsquo;ではありません。これは"
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">f</samp>&rsquo;、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">fo</"
"samp>&rsquo;、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">foo</samp>&rsquo;などに一致します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Regexps.html
msgid ""
"The matcher processes a &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">*</samp>&rsquo; "
"construct by matching, immediately, as many repetitions as can be found.  "
"Then it continues with the rest of the pattern.  If that fails, backtracking "
"occurs, discarding some of the matches of the &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">*</"
"samp>&rsquo;-modified construct in case that makes it possible to match the "
"rest of the pattern.  For example, in matching &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">ca*ar</samp>&rsquo; against the string &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">caaar</samp>&rsquo;, the &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">a*</"
"samp>&rsquo; first tries to match all three &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">a</"
"samp>&rsquo;s; but the rest of the pattern is &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">ar</samp>&rsquo; and there is only &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">r</samp>&rsquo; left to match, so this try fails.  The next "
"alternative is for &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">a*</samp>&rsquo; to match "
"only two &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">a</samp>&rsquo;s.  With this choice, "
"the rest of the regexp matches successfully."
msgstr ""
"マッチャーは、「<samp class=\"samp\">*</samp>」という構文を処理する際、まず見"
"つかった限りの繰り返し箇所を即座にマッチさせます。その後、パターンの残りの部"
"分へと進みます。これが失敗した場合、バックトラッキングが発生し、パターンの残"
"りの部分をマッチさせることが可能になる場合に備えて、「<samp "
"class=\"samp\">*</samp>」で修飾された構文のマッチ結果の一部が破棄されます。例"
"えば、文字列「<samp class=\"samp\">caaar</samp>」に対して「<samp "
"class=\"samp\">ca*ar</samp>」をマッチさせる際、「<samp class=\"samp\">a*</"
"samp>」は最初に3つの「<samp class=\"samp\">a</samp>」すべてをマッチさせようと"
"します。しかし、パターンの残りは「<samp class=\"samp\">ar</samp>」であり、"
"マッチさせるべきは「<samp class=\"samp\">r</samp>」のみであるため、この試行は"
"失敗します。次の選択肢は、「<samp class=\"samp\">a*</samp>」が2つの「<samp "
"class=\"samp\">a</samp>」のみをマッチさせることです。この選択により、正規表現"
"の残りの部分は正常にマッチします。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/emacs/Regexps.html
msgid "<kbd class=\"kbd\">+</kbd>"
msgstr "<kbd class=\"kbd\">+</kbd>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Regexps.html
msgid ""
"is a postfix operator, similar to &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">*</"
"samp>&rsquo; except that it must match the preceding expression at least "
"once.  Thus, &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">ca+r</samp>&rsquo; matches the "
"strings &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">car</samp>&rsquo; and &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">caaaar</samp>&rsquo; but not the string &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">cr</samp>&rsquo;, whereas &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">ca*r</"
"samp>&rsquo; matches all three strings."
msgstr ""
"は後置演算子であり、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">*</samp>&rsquo;と同様ですが、"
"直前の式に少なくとも1回は一致する必要があります。したがって、&lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">ca+r</samp>&rsquo;は文字列&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">car</"
"samp>&rsquo;および&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">caaaar</samp>&rsquo;には一致し"
"ますが、文字列&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">cr</samp>&rsquo;には一致しません。"
"一方、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">ca*r</samp>&rsquo;はこれら3つの文字列すべて"
"に一致します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Regexps.html
msgid ""
"is a postfix operator, similar to &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">*</"
"samp>&rsquo; except that it can match the preceding expression either once "
"or not at all.  Thus, &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">ca?r</samp>&rsquo; matches "
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">car</samp>&rsquo; or &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">cr</samp>&rsquo;, and nothing else."
msgstr ""
"は後置演算子であり、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">*</samp>&rsquo; と同様です"
"が、直前の式に1回だけマッチするか、あるいは全くマッチしないかのいずれかとなり"
"ます。したがって、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">ca?r</samp>&rsquo; は &lsquo;"
"<samp class=\"samp\">car</samp>&rsquo; または &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">cr</samp>&rsquo; にマッチし、それ以外にはマッチしません。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/emacs/Regexps.html
msgid ""
"<a id=\"index-non_002dgreedy-regexp-matching\"></a><span><kbd "
"class=\"kbd\">*?</kbd>, <kbd class=\"kbd\">+?</kbd>, <kbd class=\"kbd\">??</"
"kbd><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-non_002dgreedy-regexp-"
"matching\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<a id=\"index-non_002dgreedy-regexp-matching\"></a><span><kbd "
"class=\"kbd\">*?</kbd>, <kbd class=\"kbd\">+?</kbd>, <kbd class=\"kbd\">??</"
"kbd><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#index-non_002dgreedy-regexp-"
"matching\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Regexps.html
msgid ""
"are non-<em class=\"dfn\">greedy</em> variants of the operators above.  The "
"normal operators &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">*</samp>&rsquo;, &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">+</samp>&rsquo;, &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">?</samp>&rsquo; "
"match as much as they can, as long as the overall regexp can still match.  "
"With a following &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">?</samp>&rsquo;, they will "
"match as little as possible."
msgstr ""
"は、上記の演算子の非<em class=\"dfn\">貪欲</em>なバリエーションです。通常の演"
"算子 &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">*</samp>&rsquo;、&lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">+</samp>&rsquo;、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">?</samp>&rsquo; "
"は、正規表現全体として依然としてマッチできる限り、可能な限り多くにマッチしま"
"す。後続に &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">?</samp>&rsquo; がある場合、可能な限り"
"少なくマッチします。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Regexps.html
msgid ""
"Thus, both &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">ab*</samp>&rsquo; and &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">ab*?</samp>&rsquo; can match the string &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">a</samp>&rsquo; and the string &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">abbbb</samp>&rsquo;; but if you try to match them both "
"against the text &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">abbb</samp>&rsquo;, &lsquo;"
"<samp class=\"samp\">ab*</samp>&rsquo; will match it all (the longest valid "
"match), while &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">ab*?</samp>&rsquo; will match just "
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">a</samp>&rsquo; (the shortest valid match)."
msgstr ""
"したがって、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">ab*</samp>&rsquo;と&lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">ab*?</samp>&rsquo;はどちらも文字列&lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">a</samp>&rsquo;および文字列&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">abbbb</"
"samp>&rsquo;にマッチします。しかし、これら両方をテキスト&lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">abbb</samp>&rsquo;にマッチさせようとすると、&lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">ab*</samp>&rsquo;は全体（最長の有効なマッチ）にマッチし、一方"
"で&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">ab*?</samp>&rsquo;は&lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">a</samp>&rsquo;にのみマッチします（最短の有効なマッチ）。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Regexps.html
msgid ""
"Non-greedy operators match the shortest possible string starting at a given "
"starting point; in a forward search, though, the earliest possible starting "
"point for match is always the one chosen.  Thus, if you search for &lsquo;"
"<samp class=\"samp\">a.*?$</samp>&rsquo; against the text &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">abbab</samp>&rsquo; followed by a newline, it matches the "
"whole string.  Since it <em class=\"emph\">can</em> match starting at the "
"first &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">a</samp>&rsquo;, it does."
msgstr ""
"非貪欲演算子は、指定された開始位置から始まる可能な限り短い文字列にマッチしま"
"す。しかし、前方検索においては、マッチ可能な最も早い開始位置が常に選択されま"
"す。したがって、テキスト &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">abbab</samp>&rsquo; に続"
"いて改行がある箇所で &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">a.*?$</samp>&rsquo; を検索す"
"ると、文字列全体にマッチします。最初の &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">a</"
"samp>&rsquo; からマッチすることも<em class=\"emph\">可能</em>であるため、実際"
"にマッチします。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/emacs/Regexps.html
msgid ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-set-of-alternative-characters_002c-in-"
"regular-expressions\"></a> <a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-character-"
"set_002c-in-regular-expressions\"></a> <a id=\"index-bracket-expression\"></"
"a><span><kbd class=\"kbd\">[ &hellip; ]</kbd><a class=\"copiable-link\" "
"href=\"#index-bracket-expression\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-set-of-alternative-characters_002c-in-"
"regular-expressions\"></a> <a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-character-"
"set_002c-in-regular-expressions\"></a> <a id=\"index-bracket-expression\"></"
"a><span><kbd class=\"kbd\">[ &hellip; ]</kbd><a class=\"copiable-link\" "
"href=\"#index-bracket-expression\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Regexps.html
msgid ""
"is a <em class=\"dfn\">bracket expression</em> (a.k.a. <em class=\"dfn\">set "
"of alternative characters</em>), which matches one of a set of characters."
msgstr ""
"は<em class=\"dfn\">ブラケット式</em>（別名<em class=\"dfn\">代替文字集合</"
"em>）であり、文字集合のいずれかに一致します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Regexps.html
msgid ""
"In the simplest case, the characters between the two brackets are what this "
"set can match.  Thus, &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">[ad]</samp>&rsquo; matches "
"either one &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">a</samp>&rsquo; or one &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">d</samp>&rsquo;, and &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">[ad]*</"
"samp>&rsquo; matches any string composed of just &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">a</samp>&rsquo;s and &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">d</"
"samp>&rsquo;s (including the empty string).  It follows that &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">c[ad]*r</samp>&rsquo; matches &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">cr</"
"samp>&rsquo;, &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">car</samp>&rsquo;, &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">cdr</samp>&rsquo;, &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">caddaar</"
"samp>&rsquo;, etc."
msgstr ""
"最も単純な場合、2つの角括弧の間にある文字が、この集合でマッチ可能な文字となり"
"ます。したがって、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">[ad]</samp>&rsquo;は&lsquo;"
"<samp class=\"samp\">a</samp>&rsquo;または&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">d</"
"samp>&rsquo;のいずれかにマッチし、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">[ad]*</"
"samp>&rsquo;は&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">a</samp>&rsquo;と&lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">d</samp>&rsquo;のみで構成される任意の文字列（空文字列を含む）"
"にマッチします。これにより、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">c[ad]*r</samp>&rsquo;"
"は&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">cr</samp>&rsquo;、&lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">car</samp>&rsquo;、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">cdr</"
"samp>&rsquo;、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">caddaar</samp>&rsquo;などにマッチす"
"ることになります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Regexps.html
msgid ""
"You can also include character ranges in a character set, by writing the "
"starting and ending characters with a &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">-</"
"samp>&rsquo; between them.  Thus, &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">[a-z]</"
"samp>&rsquo; matches any lower-case <abbr class=\"acronym\">ASCII</abbr> "
"letter.  Ranges may be intermixed freely with individual characters, as in "
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">[a-z$%.]</samp>&rsquo;, which matches any lower-"
"case <abbr class=\"acronym\">ASCII</abbr> letter or &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">$</samp>&rsquo;, &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">%</samp>&rsquo; "
"or period.  As another example, &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">[α-ωί]</"
"samp>&rsquo; matches all lower-case Greek letters."
msgstr ""
"また、開始文字と終了文字を &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">-</samp>&rsquo; で挟む"
"ことで、文字セットに文字範囲を含めることもできます。例えば、&lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">[a-z]</samp>&rsquo; は任意の小文字の <abbr "
"class=\"acronym\">ASCII</abbr> 文字にマッチします。範囲は、&lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">[a-z$%.]</samp>&rsquo; （任意の小文字の <abbr "
"class=\"acronym\">ASCII</abbr> 文字にマッチ）や &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">$</samp>&rsquo;、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">%</samp>&rsquo; "
"あるいはピリオドのように、個々の文字と自由に混在させることができます。別の例"
"として、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">[α-ωί]</samp>&rsquo; はすべての小文字のギ"
"リシャ文字にマッチします。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd>
#: build/html/emacs/Regexps.html
msgid ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-character-classes_002c-in-regular-"
"expressions\"></a>"
msgstr ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-character-classes_002c-in-regular-"
"expressions\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Regexps.html
msgid ""
"You can also include certain special <em class=\"dfn\">character classes</"
"em> in a character set.  A &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">[:</samp>&rsquo; and "
"balancing &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">:]</samp>&rsquo; enclose a character "
"class inside a bracket expression.  For instance, &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">[[:alnum:]]</samp>&rsquo; matches any letter or digit.  See "
"<a data-manual=\"elisp\" href=\"https://www.gnu.org/software/emacs/manual/"
"html_node/elisp/Char-Classes.html#Char-Classes\">Char Classes</a> in <cite "
"class=\"cite\">The Emacs Lisp Reference Manual</cite>, for a list of "
"character classes."
msgstr ""
"また、文字セットに特定の特殊な<em class=\"dfn\">文字クラス</em>を含めることも"
"できます。&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">[:</samp>&rsquo;およびバランシング用の"
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">:]</samp>&rsquo;は、括弧式の中で文字クラスを囲み"
"ます。例えば、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">[[:alnum:]]</samp>&rsquo;は任意の英"
"字または数字にマッチします。文字クラスの一覧については、<cite "
"class=\"cite\">The Emacs Lisp Reference Manual</cite>の<a data-"
"manual=\"elisp\" href=\"https://www.gnu.org/software/emacs/manual/html_node/"
"elisp/Char-Classes.html#Char-Classes\">文字クラス</a>を参照してください。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Regexps.html
msgid ""
"To include a &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">]</samp>&rsquo; in a character set, "
"you must make it the first character.  For example, &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">[]a]</samp>&rsquo; matches &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">]</"
"samp>&rsquo; or &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">a</samp>&rsquo;.  To include a "
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">-</samp>&rsquo;, write &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">-</samp>&rsquo; as the last character of the set, tho you can "
"also put it first or after a range.  Thus, &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">[]-]</"
"samp>&rsquo; matches both &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">]</samp>&rsquo; and "
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">-</samp>&rsquo;."
msgstr ""
"文字セットに &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">]</samp>&rsquo; を含めるには、それを"
"先頭の文字にする必要があります。例えば、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">[]a]</"
"samp>&rsquo; は &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">]</samp>&rsquo; や &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">a</samp>&rsquo; にマッチします。&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">-"
"</samp>&rsquo; を含めるには、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">-</samp>&rsquo; を"
"セットの最後の文字として記述しますが、先頭や範囲の後に配置することも可能で"
"す。したがって、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">[]-]</samp>&rsquo; は &lsquo;"
"<samp class=\"samp\">]</samp>&rsquo; と &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">-</"
"samp>&rsquo; の両方にマッチします。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Regexps.html
msgid ""
"To include &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">^</samp>&rsquo; in a set, put it "
"anywhere but at the beginning of the set.  (At the beginning, it complements "
"the set&mdash;see below.)"
msgstr ""
"集合に &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">^</samp>&rsquo; を含めるには、集合の先頭以"
"外の任意の場所に配置してください。（先頭にある場合は、集合を補完します――後述"
"参照。）"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Regexps.html
msgid ""
"When you use a range in case-insensitive search, you should write both ends "
"of the range in upper case, or both in lower case, or both should be non-"
"letters.  The behavior of a mixed-case range such as &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">A-z</samp>&rsquo; is somewhat ill-defined, and it may change "
"in future Emacs versions."
msgstr ""
"大文字小文字を区別しない検索で範囲を指定する場合、範囲の両端をいずれも大文"
"字、いずれも小文字にするか、あるいはいずれも非文字にする必要があります。"
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">A-z</samp>&rsquo;のような大文字小文字が混在する範"
"囲の挙動は少々曖昧であり、今後のEmacsバージョンで変更される可能性があります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#.  /@w 
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
