# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/emacs/Regexps.html
msgid "<kbd class=\"kbd\">[^ &hellip; ]</kbd>"
msgstr "<kbd class=\"kbd\">[^ &hellip; ]</kbd>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Regexps.html
msgid ""
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">[^</samp>&rsquo; begins a <em "
"class=\"dfn\">complemented character set</em>, which matches any character "
"except the ones specified.  Thus, &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">[^a-z0-9A-Z]</"
"samp>&rsquo; matches all characters <em class=\"emph\">except</em> <abbr "
"class=\"acronym\">ASCII</abbr> letters and digits."
msgstr ""
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">[^</samp>&rsquo;は<em class=\"dfn\">補完文字集合"
"</em>の始まりであり、指定された文字以外のあらゆる文字にマッチします。したがっ"
"て、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">[^a-z0-9A-Z]</samp>&rsquo;は<abbr "
"class=\"acronym\">ASCII</abbr>の英字と数字<em class=\"emph\">を除く</em>すべ"
"ての文字にマッチします。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Regexps.html
msgid ""
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">^</samp>&rsquo; is not special in a character "
"set unless it is the first character.  The character following the &lsquo;"
"<samp class=\"samp\">^</samp>&rsquo; is treated as if it were first (in "
"other words, &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">-</samp>&rsquo; and &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">]</samp>&rsquo; are not special there)."
msgstr ""
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">^</samp>&rsquo; は、最初の文字でない限り、文字"
"セットにおいて特別な意味を持ちません。&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">^</"
"samp>&rsquo; に続く文字は、あたかも最初の文字であるかのように扱われます（言い"
"換えれば、そこでは &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">-</samp>&rsquo; や &lsquo;"
"<samp class=\"samp\">]</samp>&rsquo; は特別な意味を持ちません）。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Regexps.html
msgid ""
"A complemented character set can match a newline, unless newline is "
"mentioned as one of the characters not to match.  This is in contrast to the "
"handling of regexps in programs such as <code class=\"code\">grep</code>."
msgstr ""
"補完済み文字セットでは、改行がマッチしない文字の一つとして指定されていない限"
"り、改行にマッチします。これは、<code class=\"code\">grep</code> などのプログ"
"ラムにおける正規表現の扱いとは対照的です。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Regexps.html
msgid ""
"is a special character that matches the empty string, but only at the "
"beginning of a line in the text being matched.  Otherwise it fails to match "
"anything.  Thus, &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">^foo</samp>&rsquo; matches a "
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">foo</samp>&rsquo; that occurs at the beginning "
"of a line."
msgstr ""
"は、空文字列にマッチする特殊文字ですが、マッチ対象のテキストにおいて行頭にあ"
"る場合にのみ有効です。それ以外の場合は、何もマッチしません。したがって、"
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">^foo</samp>&rsquo;は、行頭に現れる&lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">foo</samp>&rsquo;にマッチします。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Regexps.html
msgid ""
"For historical compatibility reasons, &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">^</"
"samp>&rsquo; can be used with this meaning only at the beginning of the "
"regular expression, or after &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\(</samp>&rsquo; "
"or &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\|</samp>&rsquo;."
msgstr ""
"歴史的な互換性のため、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">^</samp>&rsquo;をこの意味で"
"使用できるのは、正規表現の先頭、または&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\(</"
"samp>&rsquo;や&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\|</samp>&rsquo;の後に限られます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/emacs/Regexps.html
msgid "<kbd class=\"kbd\">$</kbd>"
msgstr "<kbd class=\"kbd\">$</kbd>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Regexps.html
msgid ""
"is similar to &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">^</samp>&rsquo; but matches only "
"at the end of a line.  Thus, &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">x+$</samp>&rsquo; "
"matches a string of one &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">x</samp>&rsquo; or more "
"at the end of a line."
msgstr ""
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">^</samp>&rsquo;に似ていますが、行末にのみマッチし"
"ます。したがって、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">x+$</samp>&rsquo;は、行末にある"
"1つ以上の&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">x</samp>&rsquo;からなる文字列にマッチし"
"ます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Regexps.html
msgid ""
"For historical compatibility reasons, &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">$</"
"samp>&rsquo; can be used with this meaning only at the end of the regular "
"expression, or before &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\)</samp>&rsquo; or "
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\|</samp>&rsquo;."
msgstr ""
"歴史的な互換性のため、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">$</samp>&rsquo;をこの意味で"
"使用できるのは、正規表現の末尾、または&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\)</"
"samp>&rsquo;や&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\|</samp>&rsquo;の前に限られます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dt>
#: build/html/emacs/Regexps.html
msgid "<kbd class=\"kbd\">\\</kbd>"
msgstr "<kbd class=\"kbd\">\\</kbd>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Regexps.html
msgid ""
"has two functions: it quotes the special characters (including &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">\\</samp>&rsquo;), and it introduces additional special "
"constructs."
msgstr ""
"2つの機能を備えています。特殊文字（&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\</"
"samp>&rsquo;を含む）をクォートするほか、追加の特殊な構文を導入します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Regexps.html
msgid ""
"Because &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\</samp>&rsquo; quotes special "
"characters, &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\$</samp>&rsquo; is a regular "
"expression that matches only &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">$</samp>&rsquo;, "
"and &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\[</samp>&rsquo; is a regular expression "
"that matches only &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">[</samp>&rsquo;, and so on."
msgstr ""
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\</samp>&rsquo;は特殊文字をクォートするため、"
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\$</samp>&rsquo;は&lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">$</samp>&rsquo;にのみマッチする正規表現となり、&lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">\\[</samp>&rsquo;は&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">[</samp>&rsquo;"
"にのみマッチする正規表現となる、といった具合です。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><dl><dd><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Regexps.html
msgid ""
"See the following section for the special constructs that begin with &lsquo;"
"<samp class=\"samp\">\\</samp>&rsquo;."
msgstr ""
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\</samp>&rsquo;で始まる特殊な構文については、次"
"のセクションを参照してください。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Regexps.html
msgid ""
"Note: for historical compatibility, special characters are treated as "
"ordinary ones if they are in contexts where their special meanings make no "
"sense.  For example, &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">*foo</samp>&rsquo; treats "
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">*</samp>&rsquo; as ordinary since there is no "
"preceding expression on which the &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">*</"
"samp>&rsquo; can act.  It is poor practice to depend on this behavior; it is "
"better to quote the special character anyway, regardless of where it appears."
msgstr ""
"注：歴史的な互換性のため、特殊文字がその特殊な意味を成さない文脈にある場合"
"は、通常の文字として扱われます。例えば、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">*foo</"
"samp>&rsquo; は、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">*</samp>&rsquo; が作用する先行表"
"現が存在しないため、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">*</samp>&rsquo; を通常の文字"
"として扱います。このような挙動に依存するのは好ましくありません。どこに出現す"
"るかにかかわらず、いずれにせよ特殊文字をクォートする方が適切です。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Regexps.html
msgid ""
"As a &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\</samp>&rsquo; is not special inside a "
"bracket expression, it can never remove the special meaning of &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">-</samp>&rsquo;, &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">^</samp>&rsquo; "
"or &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">]</samp>&rsquo;.  You should not quote these "
"characters when they have no special meaning.  This would not clarify "
"anything, since backslashes can legitimately precede these characters where "
"they <em class=\"emph\">have</em> special meaning, as in &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">[^\\]</samp>&rsquo; (<code class=\"code\">&quot;[^\\\\]&quot;"
"</code> for Lisp string syntax), which matches any single character except a "
"backslash."
msgstr ""
"括弧式の中では &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\</samp>&rsquo; は特殊ではないた"
"め、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">-</samp>&rsquo;、&lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">^</samp>&rsquo;、または &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">]</"
"samp>&rsquo; の特殊な意味を打ち消すことは決してできません。これらの文字に特殊"
"な意味がない場合は、クォートで囲むべきではありません。&lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">[^\\]</samp>&rsquo;（Lispの文字列構文では <code "
"class=\"code\">&quot;[^\\\\]&quot;</code>）のように、バックスラッシュが特殊な"
"意味を<em class=\"emph\">持つ</em>箇所で正当にこれらの文字の前に配置され得る"
"ため、そうしても何も明確にはなりません。この式は、バックスラッシュ以外の任意"
"の1文字にマッチします。"

