# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Time-Intervals.html
msgid ""
"The timeclock package adds up time intervals, so you can (for instance) keep "
"track of how much time you spend working on particular projects.  (A more "
"advanced alternative is to use the Org Mode&rsquo;s facilities for clocking "
"time, see <a data-manual=\"org\" href=\"https://www.gnu.org/software/emacs/"
"manual/html_node/org/Clocking-Work-Time.html#Clocking-Work-Time\">Clocking "
"Work Time</a> in <cite class=\"cite\">The Org Manual</cite>)."
msgstr ""
"timeclockパッケージは時間間隔を累計するため、（例えば）特定のプロジェクトにど"
"れくらいの時間を費やしているかを把握できます。（より高度な代替手段として、"
"Org Modeの時間記録機能を利用する方法もあります。<cite class=\"cite\">The Org "
"Manual</cite>の<a data-manual=\"org\" href=\"https://www.gnu.org/software/"
"emacs/manual/html_node/org/Clocking-Work-Time.html#Clocking-Work-"
"Time\">Clocking Work Time</a>を参照してください）。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/emacs/Time-Intervals.html
msgid ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-timeclock_002din\"></a> <a "
"class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-timeclock_002dout\"></a> <a "
"class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-timeclock_002dchange\"></a> <a "
"class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-timeclock_002dworkday_002dremaining\"></"
"a> <a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-"
"timeclock_002dwhen_002dto_002dleave\"></a>"
msgstr ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-timeclock_002din\"></a> <a "
"class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-timeclock_002dout\"></a> <a "
"class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-timeclock_002dchange\"></a> <a "
"class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-timeclock_002dworkday_002dremaining\"></"
"a> <a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-"
"timeclock_002dwhen_002dto_002dleave\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Time-Intervals.html
msgid ""
"Use the <kbd class=\"kbd\">M-x timeclock-in</kbd> command when you start "
"working on a project, and <kbd class=\"kbd\">M-x timeclock-out</kbd> command "
"when you&rsquo;re done.  Each time you do this, it adds one time interval to "
"the record of the project.  You can change to working on a different project "
"with <kbd class=\"kbd\">M-x timeclock-change</kbd>."
msgstr ""
"プロジェクトに着手する際は<kbd class=\"kbd\">M-x timeclock-in</kbd>コマンド"
"を、完了した際には<kbd class=\"kbd\">M-x timeclock-out</kbd>コマンドを使用し"
"てください。これを行うたびに、プロジェクトの記録に1つのタイムインターバルが追"
"加されます。<kbd class=\"kbd\">M-x timeclock-change</kbd>を使えば、別のプロ"
"ジェクトに切り替えることができます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Time-Intervals.html
msgid ""
"Once you&rsquo;ve collected data from a number of time intervals, you can "
"use <kbd class=\"kbd\">M-x timeclock-workday-remaining</kbd> to see how much "
"time is left to work today (assuming a typical average of 8 hours a day), "
"and <kbd class=\"kbd\">M-x timeclock-when-to-leave</kbd> which will "
"calculate when you&rsquo;re done."
msgstr ""
"複数の時間間隔からデータを収集したら、<kbd class=\"kbd\">M-x timeclock-"
"workday-remaining</kbd>を使って本日の残り作業時間（1日平均8時間と想定）を確認"
"でき、<kbd class=\"kbd\">M-x timeclock-when-to-leave</kbd>を使えば終了時刻を"
"算出できます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/emacs/Time-Intervals.html
msgid ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-"
"timeclock_002dmode_002dline_002ddisplay-1\"></a> <a class=\"index-entry-id\" "
"id=\"index-timeclock_002dmode_002dline_002ddisplay\"></a>"
msgstr ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-"
"timeclock_002dmode_002dline_002ddisplay-1\"></a> <a class=\"index-entry-id\" "
"id=\"index-timeclock_002dmode_002dline_002ddisplay\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Time-Intervals.html
msgid ""
"If you want Emacs to display the amount of time left of your workday in the "
"mode line, either customize the <code class=\"code\">timeclock-mode-line-"
"display</code> variable and set its value to <code class=\"code\">t</code>, "
"or invoke the <kbd class=\"kbd\">M-x timeclock-mode-line-display</kbd> "
"command."
msgstr ""
"Emacsのモードラインに勤務時間の残り時間を表示させたい場合は、<code "
"class=\"code\">timeclock-mode-line-display</code>変数をカスタマイズしてその値"
"を<code class=\"code\">t</code>に設定するか、<kbd class=\"kbd\">M-x "
"timeclock-mode-line-display</kbd>コマンドを実行してください。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/emacs/Time-Intervals.html
msgid ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-"
"timeclock_002dask_002dbefore_002dexiting\"></a>"
msgstr ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-"
"timeclock_002dask_002dbefore_002dexiting\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Time-Intervals.html
msgid ""
"Terminating the current Emacs session might or might not mean that you have "
"stopped working on the project and, by default, Emacs asks you.  You can, "
"however, customize the value of the variable <code class=\"code\">timeclock-"
"ask-before-exiting</code> to <code class=\"code\">nil</code> to avoid the "
"question; then, only an explicit <kbd class=\"kbd\">M-x timeclock-out</kbd> "
"or <kbd class=\"kbd\">M-x timeclock-change</kbd> will tell Emacs that the "
"current interval is over."
msgstr ""
"現在のEmacsセッションを終了することが、プロジェクトでの作業を終えたことを意味"
"する場合もあれば、そうでない場合もあります。デフォルトでは、Emacsは確認を求め"
"ます。ただし、変数 <code class=\"code\">timeclock-ask-before-exiting</code> "
"の値を <code class=\"code\">nil</code> にカスタマイズしてこの確認を回避するこ"
"とも可能です。その場合、明示的に <kbd class=\"kbd\">M-x timeclock-out</kbd> "
"または <kbd class=\"kbd\">M-x timeclock-change</kbd> を指定して初めて、現在の"
"区間が終了したことがEmacsに伝わります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/emacs/Time-Intervals.html
msgid ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-timelog-file\"></a> <a class=\"index-"
"entry-id\" id=\"index-timeclock_002dfile\"></a> <a class=\"index-entry-id\" "
"id=\"index-timeclock_002dreread_002dlog\"></a>"
msgstr ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-timelog-file\"></a> <a class=\"index-"
"entry-id\" id=\"index-timeclock_002dfile\"></a> <a class=\"index-entry-id\" "
"id=\"index-timeclock_002dreread_002dlog\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Time-Intervals.html
msgid ""
"The timeclock functions work by accumulating the data in a file called <samp "
"class=\"file\">~/.emacs.d/timelog</samp>.  You can specify a different name "
"for this file by customizing the variable <code class=\"code\">timeclock-"
"file</code>.  If you edit the timeclock file manually, or if you change the "
"value of any of timeclock&rsquo;s customizable variables, you should run the "
"command <kbd class=\"kbd\">M-x timeclock-reread-log</kbd> to update the data "
"in Emacs from the file."
msgstr ""
"タイムクロック機能は、<samp class=\"file\">~/.emacs.d/timelog</samp> という"
"ファイルにデータを蓄積することで動作します。変数 <code "
"class=\"code\">timeclock-file</code> をカスタマイズすることで、このファイルに"
"別の名前を指定できます。タイムクロックファイルを手動で編集した場合や、タイム"
"クロックのカスタマイズ可能な変数のいずれかの値を変更した場合は、コマンド "
"<kbd class=\"kbd\">M-x timeclock-reread-log</kbd> を実行して、ファイルから "
"Emacs 内のデータを更新してください。"

