# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><h3>
#: build/html/emacs/Windows-Startup.html
msgid ""
"<span>I.1 How to Start Emacs on MS-Windows<a class=\"copiable-link\" "
"href=\"#How-to-Start-Emacs-on-MS_002dWindows\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span>I.1 MS-WindowsでEmacsを起動する方法<a class=\"copiable-link\" "
"href=\"#How-to-Start-Emacs-on-MS_002dWindows\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr>
#: build/html/emacs/Windows-Startup.html
msgid ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-starting-Emacs-on-MS_002dWindows\"></"
"a>"
msgstr ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-starting-Emacs-on-MS_002dWindows\"></"
"a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Windows-Startup.html
msgid "There are several ways of starting Emacs on MS-Windows:"
msgstr "MS-WindowsでEmacsを起動する方法はいくつかあります："

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ol><li>
#: build/html/emacs/Windows-Startup.html
msgid ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-runemacs_002eexe\"></a> <a "
"class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-desktop-shortcut_002c-MS_002dWindows\"></"
"a> <a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-start-directory_002c-"
"MS_002dWindows\"></a> <a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-directory-where-"
"Emacs-starts-on-MS_002dWindows\"></a> From the desktop shortcut icon: either "
"double-click the left mouse button on the icon, or click once, then press "
"<kbd class=\"key\">RET</kbd>.  The desktop shortcut should specify as its "
"&ldquo;Target&rdquo; (in the &ldquo;Properties&rdquo; of the shortcut) the "
"full absolute file name of <samp class=\"file\">runemacs.exe</samp>, <em "
"class=\"emph\">not</em> of <samp class=\"file\">emacs.exe</samp>.  This is "
"because <samp class=\"file\">runemacs.exe</samp> hides the console window "
"that would have been created if the target of the shortcut were <samp "
"class=\"file\">emacs.exe</samp> (which is a console program, as far as "
"Windows is concerned).  If you use this method, Emacs starts in the "
"directory specified by the shortcut.  To control where that is, right-click "
"on the shortcut, select &ldquo;Properties&rdquo;, and in the "
"&ldquo;Shortcut&rdquo; tab modify the &ldquo;Start in&rdquo; field to your "
"liking."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ol><li>
#: build/html/emacs/Windows-Startup.html
msgid ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-pinning-Emacs-to-Windows-task-bar\"></"
"a> From a task-bar shortcut icon, by clicking once the left mouse button.  "
"Windows versions since Vista allow you to create such shortcuts by <em "
"class=\"dfn\">pinning</em> the icon of a running program that appears in the "
"task bar.  You can do that with Emacs, but afterwards you will have to "
"change the properties of the pinned shortcut to run <samp "
"class=\"file\">runemacs.exe</samp>, <em class=\"emph\">not</em> of <samp "
"class=\"file\">emacs.exe</samp>.  You can also pin Emacs to the task bar by "
"clicking the right mouse button on its icon in the Start menu, then "
"selecting &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">Pin to taskbar</samp>&rsquo;.  Once "
"again, be sure to specify <samp class=\"file\">runemacs.exe</samp> as the "
"program to run.  You can control where Emacs starts by setting the "
"&ldquo;Start in&rdquo; field of the shortcut&rsquo;s Properties."
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ol><li>
#: build/html/emacs/Windows-Startup.html
msgid ""
"From the Command Prompt window, by typing <kbd class=\"kbd\">emacs <kbd "
"class=\"key\">RET</kbd></kbd> at the prompt.  The Command Prompt window "
"where you did that will not be available for invoking other commands until "
"Emacs exits.  In this case, Emacs will start in the current directory of the "
"Windows shell."
msgstr ""
"コマンドプロンプトのウィンドウで、プロンプトに <kbd class=\"kbd\">emacs <kbd "
"class=\"key\">RET</kbd></kbd> と入力します。この操作を行ったコマンドプロンプ"
"トのウィンドウは、Emacsが終了するまで他のコマンドを実行できなくなります。この"
"場合、EmacsはWindowsシェルのカレントディレクトリで起動します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ol><li>
#: build/html/emacs/Windows-Startup.html
msgid ""
"From the Command Prompt window, by typing <kbd class=\"kbd\">runemacs <kbd "
"class=\"key\">RET</kbd></kbd> at the prompt.  The Command Prompt window "
"where you did that will be immediately available for invoking other "
"commands.  In this case, Emacs will start in the current directory of the "
"Windows shell."
msgstr ""
"コマンドプロンプトのウィンドウで、プロンプトに <kbd class=\"kbd\">runemacs "
"<kbd class=\"key\">RET</kbd></kbd> と入力します。操作を行ったコマンドプロンプ"
"トのウィンドウは、すぐに他のコマンドを実行できるようになります。この場合、"
"Emacs は Windows シェルのカレントディレクトリで起動します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ol><li>
#: build/html/emacs/Windows-Startup.html
msgid ""
"From the Windows <code class=\"code\">Run</code> dialog (normally reached by "
"clicking the <code class=\"code\">Start</code> button).  Typing <kbd "
"class=\"kbd\">runemacs <kbd class=\"key\">RET</kbd></kbd> into the dialog "
"will start Emacs in the parent directory of the Windows equivalent of your "
"user&rsquo;s <code class=\"code\">HOME</code> directory, see <a "
"class=\"ref\" href=\"Windows-HOME.html\">HOME and Startup Directories on MS-"
"Windows</a>."
msgstr ""
"Windowsの<code class=\"code\">Run</code>ダイアログ（通常は<code "
"class=\"code\">Start</code>ボタンをクリックしてアクセスします）で、<kbd "
"class=\"kbd\">runemacs <kbd class=\"key\">RET</kbd></kbd>と入力すると、ユー"
"ザーの<code class=\"code\">HOME</code>ディレクトリに相当するWindows上のディレ"
"クトリの親ディレクトリでEmacsが起動します。詳細は<a class=\"ref\" "
"href=\"Windows-HOME.html\">MS-WindowsにおけるHOMEおよび起動ディレクトリ</a>を"
"参照してください。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ol><li>
#: build/html/emacs/Windows-Startup.html
msgid ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-invoking-Emacs-from-Windows-"
"Explorer\"></a> <a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-"
"emacsclient_002eexe\"></a> <a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-"
"emacsclientw_002eexe\"></a> Via <samp class=\"file\">emacsclient.exe</samp> "
"or <samp class=\"file\">emacsclientw.exe</samp>, which allow you to invoke "
"Emacs from other programs, and to reuse a running Emacs process for serving "
"editing jobs required by other programs.  See <a class=\"xref\" href=\"Emacs-"
"Server.html\">Using Emacs as a Server</a>.  The difference between <samp "
"class=\"file\">emacsclient.exe</samp> and <samp "
"class=\"file\">emacsclientw.exe</samp> is that the former is a console "
"program, while the latter is a Windows GUI program.  Both programs wait for "
"Emacs to signal that the editing job is finished, before they exit and "
"return control to the program that invoked them.  Which one of them to use "
"in each case depends on the expectations of the program that needs editing "
"services.  If that program is itself a console (text-mode)  program, you "
"should use <samp class=\"file\">emacsclient.exe</samp>, so that any of its "
"messages and prompts appear in the same command window as those of the "
"invoking program.  By contrast, if the invoking program is a GUI program, "
"you will be better off using <samp class=\"file\">emacsclientw.exe</samp>, "
"because <samp class=\"file\">emacsclient.exe</samp> will pop up a command "
"window if it is invoked from a GUI program.  A notable situation where you "
"would want <samp class=\"file\">emacsclientw.exe</samp> is when you right-"
"click on a file in the Windows Explorer and select &ldquo;Open With&rdquo; "
"from the pop-up menu.  Use the &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">--alternate-"
"editor=</samp>&rsquo; or &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">-a</samp>&rsquo; "
"options if Emacs might not be running (or not running as a server) when "
"<code class=\"command\">emacsclient</code> is invoked&mdash;that will always "
"give you an editor.  When invoked via <code class=\"command\">emacsclient</"
"code>, Emacs will start in the current directory of the program that invoked "
"<code class=\"command\">emacsclient</code>."
msgstr ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-invoking-Emacs-from-Windows-"
"Explorer\"></a> <a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-"
"emacsclient_002eexe\"></a> <a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-"
"emacsclientw_002eexe\"></a> 他のプログラムからEmacsを起動したり、実行中の"
"Emacsプロセスを再利用して他のプログラムが必要とする編集ジョブを処理したりでき"
"る <samp class=\"file\">emacsclient.exe</samp> または <samp "
"class=\"file\">emacsclientw.exe</samp> を使用します。<a class=\"xref\" "
"href=\"Emacs-Server.html\">Emacsをサーバーとして使用する</a> を参照してくださ"
"い。<samp class=\"file\">emacsclient.exe</samp> と <samp "
"class=\"file\">emacsclientw.exe</samp> の違いは、前者がコンソールプログラムで"
"あるのに対し、後者はWindows GUIプログラムである点です。どちらのプログラムも、"
"Emacsが編集ジョブの完了を通知するまで待機し、その後終了して起動元のプログラム"
"に制御を戻します。どちらを使用するかは、編集サービスを必要とするプログラムの"
"要件によって異なります。そのプログラム自体がコンソール（テキストモード）プロ"
"グラムである場合は、<samp class=\"file\">emacsclient.exe</samp> を使用してく"
"ださい。これにより、そのプログラムのメッセージやプロンプトが、起動元のプログ"
"ラムと同じコマンドウィンドウに表示されます。対照的に、起動元のプログラムがGUI"
"プログラムである場合は、<samp class=\"file\">emacsclientw.exe</samp> を使用す"
"るのが適切です。<samp class=\"file\">emacsclient.exe</samp> をGUIプログラムか"
"ら起動すると、コマンドウィンドウがポップアップ表示されるためです。<samp "
"class=\"file\">emacsclientw.exe</samp> が有用な代表的な場面は、Windowsエクス"
"プローラーでファイルを右クリックし、ポップアップメニューから「プログラムから"
"開く」を選択する場合です。<code class=\"command\">emacsclient</code> を起動し"
"た際にEmacsが実行されていない（またはサーバーとして動作していない）可能性があ"
"る場合は、<samp class=\"samp\">--alternate-editor=</samp> または <samp "
"class=\"samp\">-a</samp> オプションを使用してください。これにより、常にエディ"
"タが利用可能になります。<code class=\"command\">emacsclient</code> 経由で起動"
"した場合、Emacsは <code class=\"command\">emacsclient</code> を起動したプログ"
"ラムのカレントディレクトリで起動します。"

