# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Words.html
msgid ""
"To operate on words with an operation which acts on the region, use the "
"command <kbd class=\"kbd\">M-@</kbd> (<code class=\"code\">mark-word</"
"code>).  This command sets the mark where <kbd class=\"kbd\">M-f</kbd> would "
"move to.  See <a class=\"xref\" href=\"Marking-Objects.html\">Commands to "
"Mark Textual Objects</a>, for more information about this command."
msgstr ""
"領域に対して作用する操作を単語に適用するには、コマンド <kbd class=\"kbd\">M-"
"@</kbd> (<code class=\"code\">mark-word</code>) を使用します。このコマンド"
"は、<kbd class=\"kbd\">M-f</kbd> が移動する位置にマークを設定します。このコマ"
"ンドの詳細については、<a class=\"xref\" href=\"Marking-Objects.html\">テキス"
"トオブジェクトにマークを付けるコマンド</a>を参照してください。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Words.html
msgid ""
"The word commands&rsquo; understanding of word boundaries is controlled by "
"the syntax table.  Any character can, for example, be declared to be a word "
"delimiter.  See <a data-manual=\"elisp\" href=\"https://www.gnu.org/software/"
