# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Xref.html
msgid ""
"To do its job, <code class=\"code\">xref</code> needs to make use of "
"information and to employ methods specific to the major mode.  What files to "
"search for identifiers, how to find references to identifiers, how to "
"complete on identifiers&mdash;all this and more is mode-specific knowledge.  "
"<code class=\"code\">xref</code> delegates the mode-specific parts of its "
"job to a <em class=\"dfn\">backend</em> provided by the mode; it also "
"includes defaults for some of its commands, for those modes that don&rsquo;t "
"provide their own."
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">xref</code>がその機能を果たすには、情報を活用し、メ"
"ジャーモード固有の手法を用いる必要があります。どのファイルから識別子を検索す"
"るか、識別子への参照をどう見つけるか、識別子をどう補完するか――こうしたすべて"
"がモード固有の知識となります。<code class=\"code\">xref</code>は、機能のうち"
"モード固有の部分を、モードが提供する<em class=\"dfn\">バックエンド</em>に委ね"
"ます。また、独自のデフォルト値を提供していないモード向けに、一部のコマンドの"
"デフォルト値も組み込んでいます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/emacs/Xref.html
msgid ""
"A backend can implement its capabilities in a variety of ways.  Here are a "
"few examples:"
